INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (98, 9, 'Regional packs (RG-3..RG-5)', 300, 'Part 10 of the masterplan (plan 9): the regional bundles (packs) of the Steam release. Decision 110 answered RG-5 with OQ-46 folded in: every regional bundle 2000 approved, in its region''s language + en, free optional DLC, off by default, with its own bundle-scoped taxonomy; `colombia` is the pilot. This plan builds what the pilot''s runs (plan 84) need: bundle-scoped subcategories, `colombia`''s own list, the bundle target, `--translate --bundle`, and the effort measurement. Owners: `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` (superseded by bundles, D-39), `plans/22-bundles.md`.

## Builds on
- decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46), partly superseding decision 37''s "packs have no target":
  - every regional bundle 2000 approved, region''s language + en (`colombia`: es + en); free DLC (decision 66: Price model (OQ-33)); off on the configure screen (decision 33 / D-88 unchanged); the family''s save keeps base + `colombia` (D-85, D-59)
  - bundle-scoped taxonomy: names may repeat verbatim across bundles («Historia» in `base` and in `colombia`), still separate entries; the 19 `colombia` questions on `base` subcategories move to `colombia`''s own
  - pilot `colombia` 102 → 2000, effort measured ($ per approved via `qgen report --cost`; gamemaster''s review time per 100 from the review tool''s timestamps); more bundles only after a new decision with those numbers (plan 84); launch doesn''t wait (ships what `colombia` has; plan 96 updates bring the rest)
- decision 112: Pack layout (task 751, done): `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool[.<locale>].json`, missing file = pack not offered; `build/pack-media.json`.
- decision 26: launch languages es, en, de; decision 27: `colombia` keeps its voice.
- D-43 today: subcategory names and slugs unique across bundles (`categories.py`: a subcategory names its bundle); `names.<locale>.json` keyed by Spanish subcategory name; pool questions reference a subcategory by name. Decision 110 (d) ends the uniqueness.
- `review.reviewed_on` stores a date only (`authoring/server/main.py`): no timestamps for review time yet.
- `translate_selection` (qgen.py) picks `base` sources only; decision 45''s selection order applies per bundle too.
- `targets.json`: `base` only (D-53); `targets.deficits(pool, bundle, locale)` (plan 70 task 462) already takes a bundle.
- Plan 70 (cost, budget) reads this plan''s per-bundle `--cost` rows and review-time line; plan 84 task 643 (Regional pilot `colombia`: start) waits for tasks 4–7; plan 89 task 748 builds the DLC depots.

## RG mapping (15c)
- RG-1, RG-2: done as BN-2, BN-3 (D-39). RG-3 = BN-6 (plan 27 engine, plan 29 screen, plan 30 close-out) + plan 62''s `--simulate --bundles`. RG-4 = BN-11 (`qgen batch --bundle`). RG-5 = decision 110.

## Tasks
1. **RG-5 decision (OQ-46 folded in) and 15c marking** (task 749, done).
2. **Record RG-5** (task 750)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` for decision 110 (packs, 2000 per bundle, region''s language + en, off by default, bundle-scoped taxonomy, pilot and follow-up decision); D-43 and decision 37''s "packs have no target" marked "amended by"; 15c RG-5 `[x]`; OQ-46 → "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md`; `22-bundles.md` notes; `plans/project.md` in sync.
   - `qgen report --simulate`: default `--bundles` = the locale''s default game (`base` for every locale, c1); help text drops "until RG-5"; note in `16-content-target.md`.
   - `pm decision consequences 110 "…"`. No follow-up tasks: tasks 4–8 below are already in this plan.
3. **Packs as optional installs** (task 751, done; decision 112).
4. **Bundle-scoped taxonomy (decision 110 d)**
   - Identity of a category/subcategory = bundle + name (slug unique per bundle only). Pool questions already carry `bundle`; every lookup by subcategory name becomes by (bundle, name): `categories.py` (`category_of`, `bundle_of` go or take a bundle), `targets.py`, `qgen` draft/batch/report/validate, `pool_export.py`, names files (already per bundle: base''s `names.<locale>.json` and `app/data/bundles/<id>/names.<locale>.json` each key their own bundle''s names), engine (`app/client/src/engine/`: category choice, «Cambiazo» from the chosen bundle + subcategory, seen/supply counters), `supply.ts`, the simulation, review tool and stats pages (filters show the bundle when a name repeats).
   - `qgen validate`: drop "unique across bundles"; keep unique within a bundle.
   - Check: a throw-away pool with «Historia» in `base` and in `colombia` → «Cambiazo» on base «Historia» never serves a `colombia` question; `qgen validate`, `npm test`, the family''s save still loads and plays.
   - D-entry amending D-43; `directory.md`, `22-bundles.md`.
5. **`colombia` subcategories (OQ-46)** (after task 4)
   - `pm decision add` with a proposed list for the 19 questions on `base` subcategories (Historia 3, Piratas 2, Desiertos 2, Navidad 2, Mundiales de fútbol 2; Aves, Cuentos infantiles, Literatura, Islas, Reciclaje, Árboles, Deportes extremos, Museos): new or existing `colombia` subcategories (e.g. «Historia de Colombia», «Fútbol colombiano», «Navidad en Colombia», or a repeated base name), plus any subcategories the 2000-question target needs; taxonomy is the gamemaster''s. `pm task-pending-decision`, stop.
   - On the answer: `app/data/bundles/colombia/categories.json` (+ names en/de) through `qgen`; a `qgen` migration step like BN-13 moves the 19 (no hand edits of the pool); `validate` rule "a question''s subcategory is in its bundle''s list"; concept lists come from `qgen batch --bundle colombia`.
6. **Regional bundle target**
   - `targets.json`: `colombia` total 2000 with D-53''s difficulty mix scaled (or a proposed mix as pm decision if the bundle''s audience needs another); `targets.py` loader and `qgen validate` accept bundle entries; per locale (es, en) through `deficits(..., locale)`.
   - Read by `--bundle` drafting (`target_weights`) and `qgen report --bundle <id> [--locale L]` (progress vs. 2000).
   - `qgen bundle new` writes a 2000 entry for a new regional bundle (decision 110: every regional bundle).
7. **`qgen batch --translate <locale> --bundle <id>`**
   - `translate_selection` takes the bundle''s approved, translatable sources (decision 45''s order within them); merge and export write `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool.<locale>.json` (decision 112).
   - Market/rating for a regional bundle''s translation (an en player with a link to the region, decision 110 b): prompt change drafted, approved by pm decision (prompts are the gamemaster''s, decision 35: Translation prompts and markets per locale).
   - `bundles.json` `languages` gains the locale once its translations are approved: at plan 84''s en chain end, or earlier at launch (ships what `colombia` has) by a pm decision then; `qgen validate` warns when a bundle lists a locale without a pool file.
   - RUNBOOK and D-36 amended (`--translate` with `--bundle`).
8. **Pilot effort in `qgen report`**
   - Review tool stores a timestamp per verdict (`reviewed_at`, ISO time; `reviewed_on` kept); translations too.
   - `qgen report --cost`: rows per bundle ($ per approved of its `--bundle` and `--translate --bundle` runs, deficit to its target, projection) for plan 70.
   - `qgen report --review-time [--bundle <id>] [--run <run>]` (or a line in `--cost`): gamemaster''s review minutes per 100 verdicts, sessions from consecutive timestamps (gap > 10 min starts a new one); verdicts without a timestamp skipped and counted.
9. **Close-out** (task 752)
   - 15c done (superseded by 22), RG-1..RG-5 `[x]`; 22''s BN-6 per task 479; plan 84 task 643 unblocked (tasks 4–7 done); `plans/11-steam.md` S4 row notes packs (2000 per bundle, es + en, free DLC, pilot `colombia`), S5 points at task 748; task 749''s simulation numbers in `16-content-target.md`.

## Done when
- Decision 110 recorded; OQ-46 resolved; 15c RG-1..RG-5 `[x]`.
- Subcategories keyed by bundle + name; `colombia` on its own approved list, no question on a `base` subcategory.
- `colombia` target 2000 in `targets.json`, read by drafting and `qgen report`; `qgen batch --translate en --bundle colombia` works; `qgen report` shows per-bundle cost and review time per 100.
- A pack is an optional file set the game offers only when present (done); plan 89 has the DLC depot task (748).

## Out of scope
- Running the pilot and the "More regional bundles at launch?" decision (plan 84); new bundles (`mexico`, `argentina`: plan 84 adds their `qgen bundle new` + taxonomy tasks here after a "yes").
- Steam DLC app IDs, store entries and depots (S5: plan 89); Workshop and player-made bundles (own milestone, decision 66); the release budget (plan 70).', '2026-10-13T15:01:21Z', 249);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (99, 8, 'Retire the browser game and the Python game server', 450, 'Part 9 of masterplan 8. With decision 111: Steam only, the desktop build is the only game: the family''s save moves into `trivia-desktop`, the Python game server (`app/server/main.py`, `trivia`, `/api/save`, `nix build .#app`) goes, `app/` becomes Node/TS only, and workers check UI changes in a browser on a small Vite-based Node dev server instead of "`trivia` with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`". Authoring''s Python (qgen, `trivia-authoring`, `trivia-media`) stays Python but stops importing from `app/server/`.

## Binding
- decision 111: Steam only: no work, checks or docs for running outside Steam; saves per Steam user (plan 87); dev runs and agent checks keep working through an explicit dev switch. Here: the dev server and `--import-save` print the save location they use.
- decision 39: Local builds start offline?: start test skipped (Steam beta test), not failed; nothing here re-adds it.
- decision 104: Python ↔ Node/TS twins: won''t fix: the Python modules move, they aren''t synced or rewritten.
- decision 98: Browser game: corrupt or newer state/game.json: the backup behaviour survives in `FileStore`/`app/desktop/save.mjs`; the server endpoint goes.
- Dependencies: reuse Vite (already a dev dependency) and the desktop''s own modules; anything new needs a `pm decision`.
- Supersedes D-59''s bridge (`plans/decisions.md`).
- Every step leaves the per-commit checks green (`npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`).

## What exists (2026-10-13)
- `app/server/`: `main.py` (static + `/data/` + cache-only `/media` + `GET/PUT /api/save` + `POST /api/save/backup`, `save.migrate()` at start), `paths.py`, `save.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`.
- Authoring imports from `app/server/` via `authoring/tools/layout.py` (puts `app/server` on `sys.path`): `paths` (layout.py, save_file.py, categories.py), `save` (save_file.py: `load()`), `media_cache` (qgen.py, download.py, media.py, authoring/server/main.py, overview.py, media_stats.py), `http_base.BaseHandler` (authoring/server/main.py).
- `app/client/src/lib/store.ts`: `TextStore` → `ServerStore` (`/api/save`, `/api/save/backup`) and `FileStore` (desktop bridge `window.trivia.loadSave/writeSave/backupSave`).
- `app/client/vite.config.ts`: dev proxies `/api`, `/data`, `/media` to the Python server on :8000.
- `app/desktop/`: `save.mjs` (`makeSaveFile`, atomic write, `backup/`), `resolve.mjs` (`makeResolver`: dist, `/data/`, `/media` for `app://`), `main.mjs` (save dir `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` | `state/desktop/<steamid|local>/` in dev | `<userData>/save/…` packaged; `--import-save <file>` already there: writes only into an empty save, no `--force`, no backup).
- `flake.nix`: `trivia-dev` (the `trivia` command, `app/server/main.py`), package `app` (`nix build .#app`, also `default`).
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: step `nix` = `nix build .#app --no-link` (D-59).
- Family save: `state/game.json`, version 2 (the client upgrades it on load, engine/save.ts); `game.sqlite`/`flags.json` already migrated (backups only).

## Steps (in this order)

### 1. Node dev server for browser checks
- A Vite plugin in `app/client/` (like `credits.ts`), active in `vite` (dev client) and `vite preview` (built `dist/`):
  - `/data/` from `app/data/`, `/media` from the media cache (`TRIVIA_MEDIA` | repo `media/`), cache only: reuse `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` where it fits, so the rules are the desktop''s.
  - Save: dev-only middleware over `app/desktop/save.mjs` (`makeSaveFile`) and a dev-only page shim that provides the save half of the desktop bridge (`loadSave`, `writeSave`, `backupSave`), so the browser uses `FileStore`, the same Store as the desktop (no `ServerStore` needed). Not in the production bundle.
  - Save dir: `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` if set, else a fresh temp dir (never the family''s save); printed at start (`trivia dev: save <path>`). This is the dev switch of decision 111 for agent checks; plan 87''s "no Steam user = memory-only" must not apply to it.
  - Proxy to :8000 removed from `vite.config.ts`.
- One command each: `npm run dev -w app/client` (dev client) and e.g. `npm run serve -w app/client` (built client); fixed port, printed.
- Replace "walk it on `trivia` with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`" in AGENTS.md, plan files (`plans/*.md`) and open task bodies (`pm task set`).
- Done when: a fresh-save game plays through a few levels in a browser on the dev server, the save lands in the printed dir, media from the cache plays; `trivia` is still there.

### 2. `trivia-desktop --import-save <file>` and the family switch
- Extend the existing flag in `app/desktop/main.mjs` (+ `save.mjs`):
  - checks the envelope (JSON object, numeric `version`; the client upgrades v2 on load, no Python `save.migrate()` needed);
  - writes the desktop save atomically (`makeSaveFile`);
  - refuses a non-empty target without `--force`; with `--force` first copies the old save to `backup/game-import-<stamp>.json`;
  - prints source, target file (Steam user folder, `local/` or `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`) and backup path; the source file stays untouched.
- Then `pm decision add "Family save imported into trivia-desktop?"` (kind once), body: the exact command for the gamemaster (`trivia-desktop --import-save state/game.json`, run the way the family will play, Steam up or not, since the save folder is per Steam user), what to check (players, seen counters, a round plays), and that the family plays `trivia-desktop` from then on (later the Steam beta). Options: "imported, family plays trivia-desktop" (recommended) | "not yet".
- Step 4 waits for its answer: the step-4 tasks are `pm task-pending-decision` on it.
- Done when: the import works on a copy of the family save in a temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`; the decision is raised.

### 3. Authoring''s Python off `app/`
- Move into authoring (e.g. `authoring/tools/`) what authoring still imports: `paths.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`, and of `save.py` only what `save_file.py` uses (reading the save); `layout.py` stops putting `app/server` on `sys.path`; import comments updated.
- Move, don''t sync (decision 104); `trivia-authoring`, `qgen`, `trivia-media` behave as before.
- Save path for authoring (apply_flags, seen counts, `save_file.py`): the desktop''s save, not `state/game.json`: `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR/game.json` if set, else `state/desktop/<user>/game.json` (the only one, or the newest, named on stderr); `flags-applied.json` stays under `state/`. If this choice turns out not obvious, `pm decision add`.
- `app/server/main.py` keeps working from its own copies until step 4 (no shared imports across the line).
- Done when: no file under `authoring/` imports from `app/server/`; `qgen validate`, `qgen report`, `trivia-media sync --status approved --dry-run`-style check and `trivia-authoring` pages (review, flags) run; apply_flags reads a flag from a desktop save.

### 4. Deletions (wait for step 2''s decision)
- `app/server/` entirely (`main.py`, the remaining `paths.py`, `save.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`, `__pycache__`); `app/` has no `.py` left.
- `lib/store.ts`: `ServerStore`, `/api/save`, `/api/save/backup` (task 724''s backup endpoint); the store choice keeps only `FileStore` (desktop bridge or the dev server''s shim); `TextStore` merged into it if nothing else extends it.
- `flake.nix`: `trivia-dev` (the `trivia` command), package `app` and `default` pointing at it (and the `TRIVIA_STATE` wrapper); the dev shell list updated.
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: the `nix` step, its `--skip` choice and docstring row; header and manual rows that mention it.
- `state/game.json`, `game.sqlite`, `flags.json` are the family''s data: not deleted (gitignored backups).
- Done when: per-commit checks pass, `trivia-release-check --skip tag …` runs without a `nix` step, `grep -rn "api/save\|ServerStore\|app/server\|\.#app" app authoring flake.nix` finds nothing live.

### 5. Docs
- AGENTS.md Commands: `trivia` and `nix build .#app` out; the dev server in (command, port, save dir); `trivia-release-check` line without `nix build .#app`.
- README.md (how the family plays: `trivia-desktop`; import), `directory.md` (`app/server/` gone, new authoring modules, dev server files), `plans/decisions.md` (D-59 marked superseded by decision 111), `plans/01-architecture.md`, `plans/19-repo-layout.md`, `plans/12-client-engine.md`, `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (desktop as the only game; part 9 note), `plans/project.md` in sync.
- `pm decision consequences 111 …` with what changed.

### 6. Sweep of other milestones (after step 4)
- Open plans/tasks/decisions that still name `trivia` (the command), `/api/save`, `ServerStore`, `nix build .#app`, `TRIVIA_STATE` or "browser game": open task bodies with `pm task set`; a body that can''t change (running) or a plan needing new work: a follow-up task in the owning plan. Candidates found 2026-10-13: tasks 200 (plan 40), 591 and 741, 744 (plans 82/83; 741''s parity check loses its Python side), 652 (plan 85), 699, 700 (plan 93), 710 (plan 95), 719 (plan 97); plans 85, 87 (save per Steam user: the imported family save and the dev switch), 89 (builds, depots), 91, 92, 96, 98, 30 (pending decision 50: play-test in the browser → on `trivia-desktop` or the dev server: a task in plan 30 if its text needs changing). Plan 48 is revised by task 756: revise plan 48.

## Done when
- No Python under `app/`; the family''s save lives in the desktop build (step 2''s decision answered).
- Workers'' browser checks run on the Node dev server; AGENTS.md says how.
- Per-commit checks pass; `trivia-release-check` runs without the removed `nix build .#app` step.
- Owner plan files updated: `plans/18-steam-integration.md`, `plans/01-architecture.md`, `plans/19-repo-layout.md`; D-59 superseded by decision 111 in `plans/decisions.md`.', '2026-10-13T15:16:20Z', 758);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (100, 9, 'UI wording: style guides, TV-check fixes, screen gallery', 380, 'Part 13 of the masterplan (plan 9), from the gamemaster''s TV check (2026-10-13): the UI catalogs read like translations in places (German plural address, inconsistent terms, an Esc menu that says the wrong thing). This plan gives every UI locale a style guide, applies the TV-check fixes, and builds a screen gallery the gamemaster reviews per language, with flags that feed fix passes. Owner: `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` (new section "Wording and review"). Runs before plan 69''s playtest close-out (task 459: LUI-5: playtest fixes and close-out, 340), so the playtest sees the fixed wording.

## Builds on
- Plan 69 (catalogs `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de` ship; `check:literals`; joker names/keys D-91). Plan 68 (first-start language screen `LanguageScreen.svelte`, Esc menu language rows).
- `Overlay.svelte`: general column incl. `overlay.restart` (today abandon + configure screen, decision 34 consequence) and `overlay.quit` (desktop only).
- Decision 6 (throw-away Playwright walks) → decision 115: Screen gallery: how does trivia-gallery drive a browser? (nixpkgs Playwright in a flake wrapper, nothing in package.json).
- Decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements; decision 111: Steam only (desktop rows like quit exist only in the shell).
- D-59: the family''s Spanish game changes only in the strings decided here (milestone 9). D-29: colours within `--u`.

## Design
- **Style guides** `app/client/src/locales/style/<locale>.md` (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`), `.md` style of the repo (intro paragraph, then bullets):
  - Glossary: fixed terms (mode names, joker names from D-91/plan 24, «Spielleitung»/«anfitrión», level, bundle, flag, question/answer, Esc menu rows), Steam''s own terms where Steam has one (achievements: «Steam achievements» / «logros de Steam» / «Steam-Erfolge»; Steam Cloud, Steam Deck as Steam writes them per language).
  - Address: `es` ustedes/tú as the catalog uses today; `es-ES` vosotros where `es` addresses the group (plan 69); `en` you; `de`: never assume plural, infinitive style for prompts and buttons («Frage wählen», not «Wählt eine Frage»), no «ihr/euch/euer», «du» only where infinitive can''t work (decide per string, note it in the guide).
  - Buttons and prompts: verb first / infinitive, length, capitalisation, punctuation («…» for dialogs, «¡…!» in `es`), how keys are shown.
  - Bad patterns seen so far (from the TV check: plural address in `de`, «End game (set up another)», bare «achievements»); each with a wrong → right example. Guidance, not a lint.
- **Who reads them**: a line in `AGENTS.md` Rules: "Changing UI strings (`app/client/src/locales/`): read `locales/style/<locale>.md` first; new bad patterns found go into it." Same rule in `directory.md` for `locales/style/`.
- **Translation prompts**: question texts address players too (hints, wording), so `authoring/tools/prompts/locale-<l>.md` get the guide''s address and glossary (e.g. a `{style}` placeholder filled from the guide by `prompt(..., locale=)`, or a short pasted block: the task proposes one). Prompts are the gamemaster''s: the draft goes into a pm decision (like decision 35: Translation prompts and markets per locale); nothing changes before the answer.
- **TV-check fixes** (catalogs; behaviour only for the Esc menu row):
  - `de` mode name «Spielleitermodus» (`mode.gamemaster`; `en` «Gamemaster mode», `es` «Modo anfitrión» stay).
  - Achievements: every mention says «Steam achievements» / «logros de Steam» / «Steam-Erfolge» (today `customize.body`; grep all catalogs).
  - Esc menu: `overlay.restart` → «Back to main menu» / «Volver al menú principal» / «Zurück zum Hauptmenü»; it abandons the game (confirm as today) and goes to the start screen, not the configure screen (milestone 9 replaces decision 34''s "restart = configure screen"). `overlay.quit` «Quit game» / «Salir del juego» / «Spiel beenden» in its own colour: a new `--u` token (e.g. a muted red), apart from every other button, all states (focus, hover, pad).
  - `de` without plural address: every «ihr/euch/euer/wählt/habt/seid…» string rewritten per the guide (17 hits today in `de.ts`, plus imperatives without pronoun).
  - `es-ES`: override only where it differs; `es` changes only in the strings above (D-59).
- **Screen gallery** (`trivia-gallery`, decision 115):
