## Order
After parts 1–9 and 11 (all their docs tasks): 1 → 2 → 3; 4 after 2 (its drafts may start once 2''s URL and section names are fixed). Part 12 (task 910) publishes the examples via plan 119''s command and checks them from the Workshop on a second account, and confirms the store link once entered.', '2026-10-13T18:24:44Z', 909);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (122, 15, 'Modding end-to-end check and close-out', 150, 'Part 12 of masterplan 102 (milestone 15: Modding and Steam Workshop), last: proves the milestone''s "Done when" and closes it. The gamemaster publishes the four example mods with the game''s own command and loads them from the Workshop on a second Steam account, through one checklist decision; a second decision confirms the guide link on the store page; the release check gets a mods step and a Workshop row (a task in plan 104) so modding stays tested in every release; a docs pass makes the plan files, README and AGENTS.md match what was built. Workers never log in, upload or edit Steamworks; they write the checklists against the code as built and act on the answers.

## Builds on (don''t rebuild)
- Plan 112: Mod format, local mods/ and the app:// overlay (`mods.mjs`, layers, `--no-mods`, `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, `<userData>/mods/`, `mods.json`).
- Plan 114: Workshop source: subscribed items in the shell: its setup decision ("Steamworks: enable Workshop for ¡Trivia! and a second Steam account?", plan 114 task 3) provides Workshop in Steamworks, the tag list and **the second Steam account**; its task 4 checks one tiny CSS item. This plan reuses both, no new Steamworks setup.
- Plan 115: Bundles from mods (decision 128: merged `bundles.json`, `<mod id>:<id>`; decision 129: mod media credits).
- Plan 117: Code add-ons (decision 130: bridge `window.triviaShell`, `window.trivia` = mod API; decision 131: `/mods.js`).
- Plan 118: Mods screen and safe start (notice, crash marker, `mods:ready`, «Restart to apply»).
- Plan 119: Publishing: `trivia --publish-mod <folder>` (decision 132: `workshopId` in `mod.json`, first publish private); its task 3 is the gamemaster''s first real upload.
- Plan 120: Player bundle kit (decision 133: `--check-mod`, `modding/` shipped, release-check step `modkit`).
- Plan 121: Modding guide, examples and the store link (decision 134: `modding/README.md`, `modding/examples/{theme,rules-tweak,conversion}`, bundle example = `modding/template-bundle/`); its task 4 gets the store texts approved and their entry listed in task 672 or plan 95.
- Part 7''s plan (from task 906, decision 123: achievements with mods on): what an achievement does in a modded game; the checklist row follows its answer as built.
- Plan 104: Release checklist: report rows and Steam offline (task 870: `MANUAL`, steps, `failed` routing); task 786: Smoke game under the dev switch (`smoke.mjs` runs with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, temp `HOME`).
- Upload: `trivia-steam upload --branch beta` (gamemaster, plan 89).

## Wait
- Task 1 needs plans 112–121 and part 7''s plan done (their gamemaster checks included: plan 114 task 4, plan 119 task 3) and task 942: Release check: mods step and Workshop row (milestone 15) in plan 104; else stop and say which, don''t close.
- Task 2 needs plan 121 task 4 answered and applied (store texts approved, entry listed).
- Decision 111: Steam only: every check runs under Steam or the dev switch; no "without Steam" row.

## Decisions taken here
- **One checklist decision for the Workshop run (kind once)**, not one per example: the gamemaster publishes and subscribes in one session; each row = ✓/✗ + note. A ✗ becomes a follow-up task in the owning plan (routing below), not a fix here.
- **Release check: yes, two additions** (task 942 in plan 104):
  - Automated step `mods` (always, after `smoke`): `smoke.mjs --mods` plays the packaged Linux build with the shipped examples installed in the temp `HOME`''s `<userData>/mods/`. Always, not full only: a content-only patch changes `app/data/`, and the shell merges mods'' `bundles.json` with ours (decision 128), so data alone can break player bundles. Headless, no Steam login: the dev switch, as the smoke game (task 786).
  - Manual row `workshop` (full only): one Workshop subscription (the example theme from task 1) loads on the candidate under Steam; `--no-mods` in Steam''s launch options starts plain. Full only: Workshop discovery is shell code; a content-only patch ships none (plan 92''s reasoning, as plan 104''s `report` row).
  - No row for publishing: `--publish-mod` is checked by plan 119 task 3 and task 1 here; playing a candidate doesn''t publish.
- **The examples stay on the Workshop** after the check, public, under the developer account, titled «Example: …» per language as their `mod.json` names: modders see working items, the guide links them. The gamemaster may answer "private" in the checklist instead; the docs task follows the answer.
- **Store link "done"** = the approved bullet and link are live on the store page (coming-soon page counts). If the gamemaster enters them only at launch (plan 121''s timing), the decision''s answer says so and the milestone''s last task waits for launch.
- **`failed` routing:** local load, overlay, path, `--no-mods` → plan 112; Workshop list/state, second account sees nothing → plan 114; bundle example (selector mark, namespaced ids, media, credits) → plan 115; rules tweak, `window.trivia`, `/mods.js` → plan 117; mods screen, notice, safe start, restart → plan 118; publish command, progress, `workshopId`, legal agreement → plan 119; template, `--check-mod` → plan 120; examples, guide, store texts → plan 121; achievements with mods on → part 7''s plan; release-check step/row → plan 104. Once a plan is done: a new plan in milestone 15 (`pm plan add 15 …`) named after the failure.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Gamemaster: the four examples from the Workshop on a second account** — `pm decision add` (kind once) "Modding: publish the examples and load them from the Workshop on a second account", body written against the code and guide as built (commands, paths, ids checked by `grep`), rows:
   - beta: a `beta` build with all of milestone 15 uploaded (`trivia-steam upload --branch beta`, release check incl. `modkit` and `mods` green); both accounts on `beta`.
   - publish (account A, dev shell or the installed game''s executable from a terminal, Steam running): `--publish-mod` for `modding/template-bundle`, `modding/examples/theme`, `modding/examples/rules-tweak`, `modding/examples/conversion` → each prints an item URL, `workshopId` written into its `mod.json` (commit those four ids afterwards: task 3), legal agreement accepted once; `--visibility public` after a look at each page (or the gamemaster''s other choice, noted).
   - second account B (other machine, or the same machine with a Steam account switch; family sharing or beta key per plan 114''s setup): subscribe to all four, start the game: one-time notice → accept → mods screen lists four, source Workshop, state loaded after «Restart to apply»; no version warning.
   - bundle: player bundle in the selector marked player-made; a game with it on shows its questions (image question with its own media); Credits screen lists the mod''s media; flag action hidden on its questions.
   - theme: colours changed on start and question screens. Rules tweak: a new game has the extra Soplo and the reworded string in es, en, de.
   - conversion on top: the game is replaced; Esc/pad B quits; Steam launch options `--no-mods` → our game, mods screen says why; launch option removed → conversion again; conversion off in the mods screen → our game after restart.
   - safe start: none needed with real crashes; check that a start with mods leaves no `mods-start.json` behind after 20 s (path per plan 118).
   - achievements: per decision 123''s answer and part 7''s plan (e.g. an achievement unlocks or doesn''t with the rules tweak on; the mods screen line says so).
   - update: account A changes the theme''s colour, `--publish-mod … --changenote "test"`; B restarts Steam/the game: new colour (allow Steam''s update delay).
   - unsubscribe on B: gone from the mods screen after restart, save still plays (no unknown-id error).
   - answer = date + ✓/✗ per row (+ the four item ids and the visibility chosen). `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <decision>` and stop. After the answer: ✗ → follow-ups per routing; `pm decision consequences` on decisions 127 and 132 (what Steam did in practice: install folder, update delay, visibility); the item ids go to task 3.
2. **Gamemaster: guide link on the store page** (after plan 121 task 4) — `pm decision add` (kind once) "Store page: modding bullet and guide link live?", body: the approved texts from `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Modding" per language, where they go (task 672''s rows or the plan 95 task plan 121 added), the guide URL (decision 134), the Workshop item links from task 1 if public; options "live on the store page" (recommended) | "entered, live at launch" | "not yet". Pending on it; after the answer: a note in 17a''s "Modding" (date, live or at launch), `pm decision consequences` on decision 134. "entered, live at launch" → the task closes with that note and task 3 records the milestone''s store-link line as "at launch (plan 95)".
3. **Close-out docs** (after tasks 1, 2) — check what parts 1–10 wrote, fill only gaps (no duplicated prose):
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md`: "Modding" sections of plans 111, 112, 114, 115, 117, 118, 119, 120 present, top line "player-facing: `modding/README.md`"; bridge rename done everywhere it means the bridge (`grep -rn "window\.trivia\b" plans app directory.md README.md`: only mod-API uses left, historical log lines in `plans/project.md` get "(now `window.triviaShell`, decision 130)"); IPC list complete (`mods:list`, `mods:set`, `mods:notice`, `mods:restart`, `mods:ready`) and matches `preload.cjs`; Workshop facts from task 1 (install folder, update delay, what a subscriber sees).
   - `plans/01-architecture.md`: one overlay bullet (sources local → Workshop, `mods.json` order, layers top-wins then ours, `/mods.js`, merged `/data/bundles.json`, page-only rule) and the readable-build bullet (decision 124); add what''s missing.
   - `plans/11-steam.md`: Tracks table row "Modding and Steam Workshop" (milestone 15, guide `modding/README.md`); Principles: mods run in the page only, no network for mod code; Launch "Preconditions": milestone 15 done; ST-4 rows match task 942 (check, don''t rewrite).
   - `plans/project.md`: Steam track list gains `[x] Modding and Steam Workshop: readable build, mods from mods/ and the Workshop, code add-ons, mods screen, publish and check commands, player bundle kit, guide and examples (<date>, pm milestone 15, plans 102, 111–121 + part 7''s; decisions 124, 127–134)`.
   - `README.md`: how-tos of plans 119, 120, 121 present; add "Test mods locally" if missing (`mods/`, `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_DEV_WORKSHOP_DIR`, `--no-mods`, devtools `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`).
   - `AGENTS.md` "Commands": `trivia-desktop` line names `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, `TRIVIA_DEV_WORKSHOP_DIR`, `--no-mods`, `--check-mod <folder>`, `--publish-mod <folder>` (`--dry-run` without Steam); if five plans'' additions made it unreadable, one sub-bullet "mods: …"; `trivia-release-check` line names `modkit` and `mods`.
   - `directory.md`: every path milestone 15 added (`app/desktop/{mods,workshop,publish}.mjs`, `lib/mods.ts`, the mods screen, `mods/`, `modding/`, `state/desktop/mods.json`, `mods-start.json`) — `ls` each.
   - `modding/README.md` and the examples'' `mod.json`: the four Workshop item links / `workshopId`s from task 1 (if public; private → no links).
   - `pm decision consequences` on decisions 124, 127–134 (and part 7''s) where the built result differs or adds facts; check milestone 15''s "Done when" and plan 102''s against tasks 1, 2; a gap → follow-up task (or plan). Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).

## Done when
- The four examples load from `mods/` (plan 121, release-check `mods` step) and, published with `--publish-mod`, from the Workshop on a second Steam account (task 1 answered ✓, ✗ rows routed and fixed).
- The guide link is on the store page, or entered and live at launch per task 2''s answer.
- `trivia-release-check` has the `mods` step and the `workshop` row (task 942); plans 18, 01, 11, `project.md`, README and AGENTS.md describe modding as built.', '2026-10-13T18:27:55Z', 910);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (123, 8, 'Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound', 900, 'Agents (pm workers and interactive sessions) start the game for checks; it shouldn''t make noise on the gamemaster''s machine. Workers mustn''t need to remember a switch: under `PM_WORKER` (set by `pm run` and inherited by everything a worker launches) the game is muted unless the task opts in. Sound work opts in explicitly.

## Behaviour
- Muted when `PM_WORKER` or `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` is set; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` overrides both (for sound tasks).
- `trivia-desktop`: `webContents.setAudioMuted(true)` in `app/desktop/main.mjs`; prints `trivia desktop: muted (PM_WORKER)` or similar at start.
- Node dev server (`task 762`, plan 99 step 1) and `vite preview`: same env rule, passed to the page (or `?mute`); if task 762 isn''t done yet, a task here adds it there afterwards.
- Session only: never writes `muted` into the stored volumes (`trivia.volumes`, `sound.svelte.ts`); the family''s settings and the Esc-menu volume UI are unchanged.
- No `PM_WORKER`, no env: sound as today (the gamemaster''s runs).

## Telling agents
- AGENTS.md (Commands and Rules): game is muted under `PM_WORKER`; outside pm, launch with `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` unless the work is about sound; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` for sound checks.
- Open plans/tasks that need audio: say `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` in their body (`pm task set`): at least plans 32: Recorded sound effects (UI-10), 33: Recorded music loops (UI-10), the smoke game / release check if it checks audio, decisions 81/83 (the gamemaster listens: no change, but check their text).
- `trivia-release-check` smoke game: decide muted or not by what it checks; not silently.
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (dev switches) in sync.

## Done when
- A worker-started `trivia-desktop` and dev-server page are silent; with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` they play.
- A normal `trivia-desktop` start plays sound; stored volumes unchanged after a muted run.
- AGENTS.md says it; sound-related open tasks name the opt-in.', '2026-10-13T20:13:33Z', NULL);

