INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (147, 33, 'Source and convert a matched set of CC0 music loops', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/public/audio/{musica-normal,musica-pregunta,musica-enviada}.m4a (707 kB together, folder 2.8 MB), CREDITS.md rows. Matched set found: OpenGameArt ''Music loop variations'' by obscure music, CC0 (checked on the page), 3 intensity steps x 2 flavours (good/evil), 100 bpm, 4/4; Kenney has no music loops (only Music Jingles). Picks: normal = level1-step1 (good, F major), pregunta = level1-step2-evil (F minor), enviada = level1-step3-evil (F minor); normal↔question changes key only across the 600/800 ms fades, question↔submitted share key and tempo. Loops: 19.2 s = 8 bars each (step1/step2 are 4-bar sources repeated x2; just under the 20 s minimum, kept equal so the cut can continue at position mod 19.2 s). Sources had 1 extra sample (trimmed to exact bars) and a 0.09–0.14 jump at the wrap: 5 ms fade-out at each 4-bar end fixes it (decoded wrap now ≤0.03). Gain only (no dynamic loudnorm): −18 LUFS each (redoble −17.8), TP ≤ −1.3 dBTP; AAC 96k stereo 44.1 kHz. Loop points: AAC decodes 846848 samples (128 padding at the end, start aligned, offset 0) → use loopStart 0, loopEnd 19.2 for all three. Alternative for task 149 if the gamemaster wants calmer: the good step2/step3 (F major) from the same zip, same pipeline. check, test, build, qgen validate pass.', 'First task of plan 33: find one matched set of recordings for `normal`, `question`, `submitted` and put the converted files in place (plan 33 "Sources and licences", "Pipeline"). Conversion is here, not in the wiring task: downloads live outside the repo and don''t survive between runs.

- Sources: Kenney.nl CC0 first (music loops / jingles packs), then OpenGameArt CC0, Freesound CC0; D-45 allowlist only (CC0 preferred; CC BY ok with credit; no NC/ND/unknown). Download outside the repo; don''t commit zips.
- Need: one theme at three intensities (calm / tense / most tense; variants or stems), or loops close enough in key and tempo that ~80 ms cuts `question` ↔ `submitted` don''t clash.
- Convert with `nix shell nixpkgs#ffmpeg-headless`: whole number of bars, loop length 20–40 s, `loudnorm` to the same target as `redoble.m4a`, stereo ok, AAC `.m4a` ~96–128 kbit/s → `app/client/public/audio/musica-normal.m4a`, `musica-pregunta.m4a`, `musica-enviada.m4a`.
- Check the seam (AAC encoder padding); note the loop points in seconds per file in the done note if the file length isn''t clean.
- `app/client/public/audio/CREDITS.md`: one row per file (source URL, pack, author, licence), CC0 too.
- Budget: the three ≤ 900 kB together; whole folder ≤ 3.5 MB.
- No matched set found: don''t guess. `pm decision add` for the gamemaster with the candidates you found and the options from plan 33 (1. one CC0 loop for all three, varied by rate / low-pass / synth layer on top; 2. recordings for some tracks, synth for the rest; 3. keep the synthesized loops), your recommendation first; make this task and the wiring task pending on it, stage, stop. After the answer: convert what the chosen option needs.

Done when: the three files (or what the decision asks for) are in place, within budget, with credit rows; the done note lists source, key, tempo, loop points.', '2026-10-12T00:36:37Z', '2026-10-13T06:46:09Z', 139);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (148, 33, 'Wire the music loops into startTrack() with synth fallback; extend /?efectos', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts, EffectsDemo.svelte: SAMPLE_NAMES + musica-normal/-pregunta/-enviada; startTrack() plays the decoded loop (loop=true, loopEnd 19.2, MUSIC_LEVEL 1.6 — a guess, tune by ear in task 149) and waits for the samples after the unlock, so the Start screen gets the recording; generated scheduler (generate()) stays as the fallback. question↔submitted cuts continue at the old loop''s position (same tempo/length; decide by ear in task 149, set offset undefined to start at 0). music(track, {synth}) for /?efectos: per-loop «grabado»/«sintetizado», «corte», «parar». Headless Chrome check: recordings start looped (19.2 s), cut offset carried over, blocked files → generated loops. check, test, build, qgen validate pass.', 'Play the recorded loops from the previous task (plan 33 "Wiring", "Audition aid").

- `app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts`: `SAMPLE_NAMES` gets `musica-normal`, `musica-pregunta`, `musica-enviada`; `startTrack()` plays the decoded buffer via `AudioBufferSourceNode` with `loop = true` (+ `loopStart`/`loopEnd` per track if the previous task''s note gives loop points) into the track''s gain, like the `redoble` branch. The lookahead scheduler (`CHORDS`, `TEMPO`) stays as the fallback when a file is missing or fails to decode.
- Behaviour unchanged (04 "Music"): 600/800 ms fades, ~80 ms cuts `question` ↔ `submitted`, cut to `roll` on submit, ducking for jokers.
- Cuts: if the loops share tempo, start the new one at the old one''s position modulo its length so the beat continues; else at 0. Decide by ear.
- A per-track level constant if they don''t sit right against the music bus (as `redoble` uses 2.2).
- `/?efectos` (plan 32''s list in `Game.svelte`): the three tracks with «grabado» / «sintetizado», a «corte» button toggling `question` ↔ `submitted`, tracks keep looping so the seam can be heard.
- Header comment of `sound.svelte.ts`: what is still synthesized.
- If the decision from the previous task chose another option, implement that instead (e.g. one loop varied by rate / low-pass / synth layer).

Done when: `npm run check`, `npm run build` pass; dev browser: the three loops play gapless, cuts and fades work; with the files removed the synth loops play.', '2026-10-12T00:36:37Z', '2026-10-13T06:49:21Z', 139);
