INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (222, 44, 'Action layer core; Game, Overlay and Player on actions (IN-2)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12: app/client/src/lib/input.svelte.ts (new; .svelte.ts because lastDevice is $state): Action (+device), toIntent keymap (scope extras via pushScope keys), scope stack (modal above non-modal, whileBusy, text fallback, temporary raw passthrough), dispatch, listen (keydown, pointerdown = mouse, click/key unlock audio). Game.svelte: global game scope (menu/flag) + one scope per screen, question via raw passthrough to Question.key (task 223 removes it); Overlay.svelte and Player.svelte (+ delete dialog, modal) push scopes, key()/dialogOpen() exports gone. Checked: npm run check/build, throw-away keymap+scope script, headless Chrome on a temp state: Start Enter/N, Player 1-9/letter→field/Enter/Esc/delete dialog Esc+Backspace, Level/Select/Question/Wrong, flag M, overlay ↑↓←→ Enter ¿Seguro? Esc. Not covered: Victory (same handler as Wrong). Remaining keydown users: Question, CategoryPicker (task 223).', 'Plan 44, task 1; design in the plan body ("Design" → `lib/input.ts`). Client only; never edit `lib/api.ts` or the data flow (PORT-7 coordination).

- New `app/client/src/lib/input.ts`, no dependency: `Action` type (confirm, back, menu, pick n 1–9, joker, navigate dir, replay, flag, new) with `device`; `lastDevice` `$state` (pointerdown = mouse); keymap with per-scope extras (`question`: A–D, joker letters read from `TOKENS`/catalog, never copied, R; `start`: N); scope stack `pushScope({ name, keys, handle, root?, modal? })` → pop; `text` handling (input focused: only Enter/Esc/↑↓ become actions; a letter outside the Player field focuses it); `e.repeat` ignored, first key/click unlocks audio, `busy` drops all but menu/flag, `preventDefault` when handled; `dispatch(action)` export for part 5.
- The single `svelte:window` key listener moves from `Game.svelte` into `input.ts` (or Game calls its handler).
- `Game.svelte`: one scope per screen (start, level, select, correct, wrong, victory) plus global menu/flag; replaces the `overlayOpen`/`dialogOpen()` chain.
- `Overlay.svelte` (menu = close, modal) and `Player.svelte` incl. delete dialog (modal, menu = back) push their own scopes; their `key(e)` exports go.
- Question and Cambiazo keep the raw event via a temporary passthrough scope (removed in task 2).
- Mouse: `onclick` stays; click and action call the same function.

Check: `npm run check`, `npm run build`; throw-away script for key + scope → action; in the browser (`trivia` + `npm run dev -w app/client`) every key of `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Input" on Start, Player, Level, Select, Correct, Wrong, Victory and the overlay does what it did.', '2026-10-12T01:04:36Z', '2026-10-12T05:39:11Z', 217);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (223, 44, 'Question, jokers and Cambiazo on actions (IN-2)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12: Question.svelte pushes scopes (question: A–D/1–4 pick, joker letters from TOKENS, Backspace unlock, Enter/Space submit, R replay; question-armed: Enter fire, Esc/Backspace disarm; question-skip modal: 1/2, Esc/Backspace; question-snipe modal: letters/digits aim, arrows moveTarget, Enter shoot, Esc/Backspace cancel); CategoryPicker.svelte pushes a modal cambiazo scope (Esc cancel, Backspace back, arrows move; Enter/Space stay native); key()/dialogOpen() exports, the picker ref and task 222''s raw passthrough (input.svelte.ts, Game.svelte) removed; plans/14-input.md IN-2 [x]. Checked: npm run check/build; grep keydown|KeyboardEvent lists only lib/input.svelte.ts; headless Chrome via CDP on a temp state: lock/unlock (letters, digits, Backspace, tap again), final + Space submit, replay, M flag, Soplo arm/Esc/Backspace/Enter, Bájale unavailable ignored, Francotirador arrows/letters/digits aim, M and joker keys ignored while aiming, Esc cancel, Enter shot; Paso Esc/Backspace cancel, 1 and 2 (purge) fire; Cambiazo arrows, Enter/Space open, Backspace back (focus kept) and cancel, Esc cancel without overlay, pick swaps; overlay Esc, skip and undo from the question. Difference: M while a joker is armed now flags (before: ignored).', 'Plan 44, task 2; needs task 1 (`lib/input.ts`).

- `Question.svelte` pushes scopes for answering, armed joker, Paso dialog (modal, pick 1/2), Francotirador (handles navigate itself via `moveTarget`, letters aim), Cambiazo (`CategoryPicker.svelte`: Esc cancel, Backspace back a level, arrows still move over tiles).
- Remove the `key(e)` exports of Question and CategoryPicker and task 1''s passthrough scope.

Check: `npm run check`, `npm run build`; `grep -rn "keydown\|KeyboardEvent" app/client/src` lists only `lib/input.ts`; in the browser every joker (incl. unavailable ones), Paso 1/2, aim with letters and arrows, unlock, replay, submit, flag, undo/skip from the overlay work as before. Mark `IN-2` `[x]` in `plans/14-input.md`.', '2026-10-12T01:04:36Z', '2026-10-12T05:45:04Z', 217);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (224, 44, 'Spatial focus, ring and memory (IN-3)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12: app/client/src/lib/focus.ts (new: nearest() rect rule, candidates, navigate with default/memory, press, opener, Tab/pointer tracking); lib/input.svelte.ts (confirm presses the shown control in the top scope''s root, else the scope''s default; unhandled navigate → spatial focus in the top rooted scope, never below a modal; Scope.root/keep; memory cleared on push except Start; modal scopes give focus back to their opener; focusControl(); Tab tracked in the one keydown listener); Game/Question/Player/CategoryPicker roots + data-focus-default/-id, data-nofocus on ☰ and flag, Game no longer pushes a question scope; CategoryPicker.move removed (generic spatial: no wrap at row ends, goes diagonal past disabled tiles, reaches Atrás/Cancelar); Player delete dialog focuses «Cancelar» after its scope is pushed. Ring: [data-nav] attribute (theme.css + :global([data-nav]) next to each :focus-visible rule). A class didn''t survive Svelte class updates, and Chromium 155 ignores focus({focusVisible:true}) after a mouse click; the attribute doesn''t depend on the browser (Firefox not installed here, not checked). Differs from plan 44: the rule is edge distance + 2 × cross-axis gap, with controls in line (cross-axis overlap) first and ties to the nearer centre; plain centre distance chose the final button over C from D and went diagonal past disabled Cambiazo tiles. Checked: npm run check/build; grep keydown|KeyboardEvent lists only input.svelte.ts; throw-away rect script (2×2 answers + final, 4 cards, 6×3 Cambiazo with disabled tiles, Player names with delete badges); headless Chrome via CDP: Start/Level/Select/Wrong defaults, cards ←→, answers 2×2, tray tokens ↑↓, Enter on a focused answer locks it, mouse-locked answer + Enter submits as today, overlay Esc keeps the ring, Paso dialog arrows + Esc gives focus back, Soplo S+Enter with ring on an answer fires (no lock), Cambiazo arrows/Enter/⌫/Esc, Francotirador arrows, Player name → delete badge → dialog «Cancelar» default → Esc back to the badge, input ↑, Tab sets the ring and Enter presses it. For task 225: Enter on a ring-focused locked answer unlocks it (to submit, ↓ to «Respuesta final»); ↓ from the last tray token jumps to answer A.', 'Plan 44, task 3; design in the plan body ("Focus navigation"). Needs tasks 1–2.

- New `app/client/src/lib/focus.ts`: pure rect function (primary distance + 2 × cross offset, no wrap) plus `navigate(dir)` over candidates in the top scope''s `root` (enabled `button`, `input`, `a[href]`, `[data-focusable]`; never `tabindex="-1"`/`[data-nofocus]`).
- `data-nofocus` on ☰ and flag (stay `tabindex="-1"`); `data-focus-default` on «¡Jugar!»/«Continuar», «Seguir», first card, first answer, «Cancelar» in the delete dialog; `data-focus-id` where index isn''t stable.
- First navigate with nothing focused focuses the default; `confirm` clicks the focused control only if focus came from navigate/Tab, else the screen''s default (Enter as today).
- Ring: sky outline from `theme.css` on every candidate; find out whether `focus({ focusVisible: true })` or a `.nav-focus` class shows it in Chromium and Firefox, use what works.
- Focus memory per scope name, restored when the scope is on top again, cleared on new content; dialogs return focus to their opener.
- Cambiazo: `CategoryPicker.move` uses the helper if it gives the same result. Overlay and Francotirador keep handling navigate themselves.

Check: throw-away script for the rect logic (2×2 answers, 4 cards, Cambiazo grid with disabled tiles); in the browser every screen and dialog plays with arrows + Enter + Esc/Backspace, the ring is visible wherever focus is, Enter without arrows behaves as today.', '2026-10-12T01:04:36Z', '2026-10-12T05:54:53Z', 217);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (225, 44, 'Audit, docs and later screens (IN-3)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12: lib/input.svelte.ts + lib/focus.ts (Scope.pressable: Enter on a ring-focused locked answer submits instead of unlocking), Question.svelte (pressable), Game.svelte (data-focus-default on Wrong and Victory); plans/04-ui-tv-display.md (Input rule: actions, focus default, no keydown elsewhere), plans/14-input.md IN-3 [x], plans/project.md IN-2/IN-3, directory.md (input.svelte.ts, focus.ts). Walked in headless Chrome with keys only: Start → Player (typed new name, delete dialog Cancelar/Sí, Esc) → Level → Select (cards ←→) → answers (lock with Enter, Enter again submits) → Wrong and Correct → every available joker via the ring (Soplo arm+fire, Paso dialog + Esc back to its token, Cambiazo grid/⌫/Esc, Francotirador aim + shoot) → overlay (undo, skip, restart with ¿Seguro?, volumes, mute, joker preset and steppers). Victory not reached (same markup as Wrong). Kept: ↓ from the last tray token goes to answer A (nearest below, not wrap); disabled tokens (e.g. Bájale at level 1) are skipped by arrows. Plans 29/36: no Choice, report or settings screen yet; follow-ups tasks 347 (plan 29, prio 390), 348 and 349 (plan 36, prio 480/370). TV check at the next game night: the family''s keys as before (A–D/1–4, Enter, Backspace unlock, S P F T X, R, M, Esc, N on Start, number keys on Player); then arrows only: ↓ shows the ring on «¡Jugar!»/«Seguir»/first card/answer A, Enter presses it, Enter on the locked answer submits, arrows reach the joker tray left of the answers, Esc/Backspace close every dialog; a mouse click never steals Enter.', 'Plan 44, task 4; needs tasks 1–3.

- Walk a full game with arrows + Enter + Esc/Backspace only: start → player (new name, delete) → levels → every joker → wrong and victory → overlay (undo, skip, restart, volumes, jokers). Fix what''s missing.
