  - Windows x64, Linux x64: fullscreen on the gamemaster''s screen, Steam client running.
  - Deck-sized: the Linux build in a 1280×800 window, pad only (decision 125); intro says how to get that window.
  - Rows per platform (plan 48 "The checklist"):
    - Start: fullscreen, no launcher or console window; F11/menu toggles windowed and back (Deck-sized: the window at 1280×800 instead).
    - Controller only (keyboard and mouse unplugged; Xbox-style pad): new player via the letter picker; pick an existing player; play to level 12 or a loss.
    - Every joker once incl. Paso dialog, Francotirador aim, Cambiazo both levels; ☰ overlay via Start (volume, presets); every dialog closes with B.
    - Glyphs match the pad (Xbox; PlayStation if at hand); after a key press keyboard prompts, back on a pad press.
    - Media: image, video and audio question play; music and sounds audible.
    - Image peek: on an image question, holding R3 shows the whole picture with every panel hidden; release brings the UI back unchanged (focus, locked answer, armed joker); same with `V` held on the keyboard; the RS / R3 prompt shows only on image questions; no peek on video/audio questions.
    - Credits screen opens and scrolls with the pad.
    - Save: quit mid-game and restart → players and seen counters kept; force-quit and restart → same.
