INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (410, 62, 'Simulation core: sim/load.ts and sim/simulate.ts for solo and rr-coop', 'work', 'done', 570, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/sim/{load.ts,simulate.ts,package.json}. Check (es, all bundles, 50 seeds; games per player median/p10, bottleneck level): kids strong 27/24 L1, typical 27/24.9 L1; young_teens strong 28/25 L1, typical 27/25 L1; young_adults strong 36/35.9 L10, typical 78.5/71.9 L6; adults strong 28/26.9 L11 (12–15), typical 68/60.8 L5. Adults ≈28, not D-76''s ≈8: model, not bug — the engine burns only the answered card (1 of 4 shown), D-76''s estimate counted shown cards (level_weights = 3 × cards per game). Kids/young_teens bottleneck = level 1 (difficulty 1: 36 approved, one burned per game). Run time 255 s for 8 cells × 50 seeds (15–50 s per cell): task 412 must lower default seeds (~10) to stay under ~1 min. npm run check passes (sim files not in it: no @types/node; tsc on them shows only missing node types). No deps, state/ untouched.', 'Part 1 of plan 62 (CT-2). Follow plan 62, "Design", Node side. Information only; no Python yet (task 3).

- New `authoring/tools/sim/load.ts`: reads `app/data/` (pool for a locale: `pool.<locale>.json`, `es` falls back to `pool.json`; categories incl. `bundles/<id>/categories.json`, `bundles.json`, `age-groups.json`) → `EngineData` (`state.ts`). Export one function; it''s the loader every Node entry point uses (plan 51''s `authoring/tools/supply.ts`, task 300, may switch to it). Missing pool → a clear `no_pool` result, not a crash.
- New `authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts` (`node authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts`): JSON on stdin (`locale`, `bundles`, `age_group`, `mode`, `player` `strong|typical`, `seeds`, `seed`), JSON on stdout. Imports `../../../app/client/src/engine/*.ts` with `.ts` extensions, erasable syntax only, only `node:` built-ins (D-60).
- Referee = the engine: one in-memory `SaveData` (`emptySave`) per seed, `Io` with a seeded `Rng` (D-58) and a fixed `now`. Loop `newGame` → `pick` (random of the cards) → joker per policy → `answer` until `newGame` throws `supply_short`; count finished games.
- `rr-coop` = `solo` (same burns, D-77; `BUILT_MODES` lacks it, so run the engine as `solo` and label the result `rr-coop`).
- Player models: `strong` (always right) and `typical` (p(level) linear 0.95 → 0.6, a named constant, returned in the output header).
- Joker policy (`STANDARD_JOKERS`): each joker once at a random allowed level; a refused joker (any `GameError`) is skipped. Use the engine''s joker functions, no rule copy.
- Output: per seed games count; median, p10, strong bound (min over seeds of `strong`); bottleneck = first `missing` level of the `supply_short` error → level, difficulty range, top 3 subcategories with no candidates left at it.

Check (throw-away script, deleted afterwards): today''s `app/data/pool.json`, `es`, every bundle, each age group, both players, 50 seeds. Adults should land roughly near D-76''s ≈ 8 games per player; note the numbers and the run time in the done note. If far off, find out why before closing (bug vs model).

Done when: the check runs, `npm run check` passes, no new dependencies, `state/` never written.', '2026-10-12T17:56:16Z', '2026-10-12T18:03:10Z', 409);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (411, 62, 'Simulation: rr-competitive and timed models (--players N)', 'work', 'done', 560, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts: input players (default 4 for rr-competitive/timed). rr-competitive = N solo engine games per session, each game''s burns turned global (player_id null, D-28); comment: until MD-8. timed (until MD-9, D-80): round = level, selection.draw with n = players still in, age-group ranges + bundle filter from resolveChoice, burned for all, no jokers; typical drops on a wrong answer, strong nobody; game ends at one left; stops when a round can''t be drawn. Check (es, adults, 10 seeds, median games per player, bottleneck level): solo strong 28 L11, typical 64.5 L5; rr-competitive N=2 strong 14 / typical 32, N=4 strong 7 / typical 16 (≈ solo/N, bottleneck as solo); timed N=2 strong 17 / typical 59.5, N=4 strong 9 / typical 23, bottleneck L1 (adults'' level 1 = difficulty 5 only, N burned per game there vs 1 in solo). ~6-8 s per rr cell, ~1 s per timed cell. npm run check passes (sim files outside it; standalone tsc shows only missing Node types).', 'Part 2 of plan 62. Needs task 410 done. Follow plan 62, "Modes", in `authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts`.

- Input gets `players` (default 4 for these modes).
- `rr-competitive`: N player names in one save; a session = N `solo` engine games, one per player; every question shown (cards picked, joker swaps) is written as burned for all N players. Games per player = sessions until any player''s `newGame` throws `supply_short`. Reuse the engine''s burn path; no rule copy. Comment: replace with the engine''s mode once MD-8 lands.
- `timed` (MD-9 not built): up to 12 rounds, N questions per round drawn with `selection.draw` at the round''s level ranges (respect the age-group windows and bundle filter from `resolveChoice`), burned for all N players; no jokers. Drop-outs: `typical` p(level) per player, `strong` = nobody drops out; the round count shrinks as players drop. Stop when a round can''t be drawn. Comment: replace with the engine''s `timed` once MD-9 lands.
- Same output shape and bottleneck as task 410.

Check (throw-away script): N = 2 and 4, both players, adults, today''s pool; games per player for rr-competitive < solo, timed bottleneck plausible. Note the numbers in the done note.

Done when: the check runs, `npm run check` passes.', '2026-10-12T17:56:16Z', '2026-10-12T18:05:25Z', 409);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (412, 62, 'qgen report --simulate: matrix, table, target check, docs (CT-2)', 'work', 'done', 550, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/engine.py (new), authoring/tools/qgen.py (report --simulate: matrix in parallel node processes, table, --json, D-75 target check exit 1; default seeds 40, default matrix 56 s), AGENTS.md, plans/16-content-target.md (Metric, CT-2 [x]), plans/project.md', 'Part 3 of plan 62. Needs tasks 410 and 411 done. Follow plan 62, "Python side" and "Docs".

