Checks: `qgen report`, `qgen validate`, `trivia-authoring` start page with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` holding a v2 and a v3 `game.json` (asserted before the server starts); never write `state/`.', '2026-10-12T18:27:24Z', '2026-10-12T19:07:47Z', 418);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (426, 65, 'CT-2 simulation with seen counts', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts, authoring/tools/qgen.py, plans/16-content-target.md, plans/backlog.md: simulation on one v3 save, engine draw by seen count, D-28 workarounds gone; stops at the first game whose level draw repeats, max 500 games (capped seeds reported). Headline = games until the first repeat (any card); Cambiazo into thin subcategories causes nearly all early repeats (adults strong 12 vs level draw 26), so there are extra columns: cambiazo seeds and draw median/bound, plus k. --json: games{…,cambiazo}, draw{…,capped}, k, repeat (was bottleneck), max_games. --mode all --seeds 2: 32 cells in 9 s. Strong draw vs k: adults 26/30, young_adults 36/36, rr-competitive adults 6/7 and young_adults 8.5/9; kids 9.5/24 and young_teens 17.5/24 (greedy draw, B-16); timed 9–11 vs 32–49 (outlook counts 1 question per round, B-15).', '`qgen report --simulate` (`authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts`, plan 62) still burns. Plan 65, "Also".

