INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (443, 67, 'Server: locale in the question API', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/server/main.py (GET ?locale=, review/difficulty with locale, translatable route, refusals, docstring), authoring/tools/qgen.py (translation_audit_of); no media-text route per decision 35', 'Plan 67, task 1 (QT-4, server side). Files: `authoring/server/main.py` (+ `authoring/tools/translations.py`, `qgen.py` if a helper is missing).

- `GET /api/questions?locale=<l>` (`l` in `translations.LOCALES`; `es` or absent = today, byte-identical): one item per entry of `questions.<l>.json`: the source question (id, `subcategory`, `bundle`, `media`, `background`, `translatable`, candidates) with the translation''s text fields, `difficulty`, `status`, `batch`, `review`, `media_text`; plus `source` (Spanish text fields, `difficulty`, `status`) and `stale` (`translations.is_stale`).
  - Filters: `batch`, `status`, `reviewer`, `sample`, `audit` on the translation; `bundle`, `subcategory`, `media` on the source; `stale=1` only stale ones.
  - `audit`: the translation''s own (`work/<t.batch>/audit/<id>.json`), never the source''s back-audit (`qgen.audit_of` takes the batch, or a locale-aware sibling).
- POST with `"locale"` in the body: `review`, `difficulty`, `difficulty_original` write the locale file through `translations` (one lock, re-read, atomic save, then `translations.exports` → `app/data/pool.<l>.json`); same rules and undo as the source (D-32/D-33: human decision replaces the LLM review, keeps it as `previous`).
- New `POST /api/questions/<id>/media-text` `{"locale", "media_text": bool}`.
- New `POST /api/questions/<id>/translatable` `{"translatable": bool}`: sets the source''s flag (not a text field, no staleness, plan 63); with `false`, non-rejected translations of that id become rejected with feedback "no viaja" (validate''s rule); re-export Spanish and locale pools.
- `media`, `media/search`, `bundle` with a locale → 400.
- Docstring API lines for every new parameter and route.
- Plan 66''s shapes (tasks 438–440) may not exist yet: build against them as described in plan 67.

Done when: on a git worktree with a throw-away `authoring/data/questions.en.json` of 3 entries (fresh, stale, non-translatable source), `curl` shows GET with filters, each POST writing the locale file and `pool.en.json`, undo restoring, the refusals; `qgen validate` clean; Spanish GET and `pool.json` unchanged (D-59). Worktree discarded.', '2026-10-12T19:34:43Z', '2026-10-13T00:37:18Z', 442);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (444, 67, 'Review page: translation side by side', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/ui/src/review/Review.svelte (?locale=, locale switch, stale banner, no approve when stale, doesn''t travel + undo, media/bundle keys refused), new SourcePanel.svelte (Spanish source | translation row by row), MediaPanel.svelte (readonly), lib/api.ts + types.ts (locale, setTranslatable, fetchNames), authoring/server/main.py (GET /api/names?locale=); verified on a worktree with a throw-away questions.en.json: approve, difficulty, doesn''t travel write the locale file and pool.en.json, undo restores, qgen validate OK, pool.json unchanged', 'Plan 67, task 2 (QT-4, UI). Files: `authoring/ui/src/review/Review.svelte`, new `SourcePanel.svelte` (keep `Review.svelte` from growing). Needs the API of the plan''s server task.

- `?locale=en|de`: header shows the locale; locale switch (es · en · de) keeps the other params.
- Left: Spanish source, read-only, with its difficulty and status; right: the translation; rows aligned (question, answer, wrong answers, hints, description, fun fact).
- Stale translation: banner, no approve (the next `--translate` run redoes it).
- Subcategory and bundle with the locale''s names (`names.<locale>.json`, via an API field or the existing names route) plus the Spanish key.
- Same verdicts, feedback, problem toggles, difficulty, undo, keyboard keys as the Spanish view, posting with `locale`.
- Media: shown, not pickable; link to `/review?id=<id>` to change the source''s media.
- "Doesn''t travel" button: `translatable: false` with confirm; a source with `translatable: false` shows it and allows undoing.
- Spanish view unchanged.

Done when: `npm run check`, `npm run build` clean; on a worktree with the throw-away `questions.en.json` (as in the server task), clicking through `/review?locale=en` writes the locale file and `app/data/pool.en.json` for a decision, a difficulty change and doesn''t-travel; undo restores; `qgen validate` clean. Worktree discarded.
- No `media_text` toggle: decision 35 dropped the flag (text in media is never a problem); the server has no media-text route (task 443).', '2026-10-12T19:34:44Z', '2026-10-13T00:40:59Z', 442);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (445, 67, 'Spot check per locale (tr-* runs)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/server/spot_checks.py, authoring/server/main.py, authoring/tools/qgen.py, authoring/ui/src/review/SourcePanel.svelte, Review.svelte', 'Plan 67, task 3 (QT-4, plan 16''s spot check for translations). Files: `authoring/server/spot_checks.py`, `main.py`, the review page, `qgen validate`''s spot-check check in `authoring/tools/qgen.py`.

