INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (461, 70, 'qgen report --cost: $/approved per run kind and projection per language (CT-3)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/qgen.py (report --cost [--json]), AGENTS.md, plans/16-content-target.md Cost: batch-4..7 0.16/0.37/0.30/0.24 match batches.md; draft $0.26, overhead ratio 0.70, es ~$1750 to go, en/de no pilot yet', 'Plan 70 design "Cost report (CT-3)". `qgen report --cost [--json]` in `authoring/qgen.py`, reusing `costs()` and the `health` metrics.

- Per run (`batch-*`, `tr-<L>-*`, `rework-*`, `tighten-*`, `neutralize-*`, `concepts`, others): calls, $ (incl. `work/<run>/audit/costs.log`), approved, $ per approved.
- Per kind: draft $/approved (last 3 `batch-*`, weighted by approved), translation $/approved per locale (`tr-<L>-*`), overhead ratio = non-batch $ / batch $.
- Projection per launch language (`es`, `en`, `de`, decision 26): deficit × $/approved × (1 + overhead ratio). `en`/`de`: "no pilot yet" until a `tr-<L>-*` run exists. Until task 2 lands, deficit = `targets.deficits()` for `es` and the full target for `en`/`de`; task 2 swaps in per-locale deficits and the `es` source shortfall.
- Spent vs. budget per language when `targets.json` has `"budget"` (task 3); information only, no stop (D-55).
- `work/` is local and gitignored: print which runs/logs were missing or skipped.
- AGENTS.md `qgen report` line; plan 16 "Cost": today''s numbers.

Done when: `qgen report --cost` and `--json` run on the local `work/`; batch-4..7 $/approved match `authoring/reports/batches.md` (0.16 / 0.37 / 0.30 / 0.24); `npm run check` / `qgen validate` still pass.', '2026-10-12T19:46:44Z', '2026-10-12T19:48:29Z', 460);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (462, 70, 'Per-locale deficits and es source shortfall (CT-4)', 'work', 'done', 550, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/{targets,translations,qgen,batches}.py, plans/decisions.md (D-84), plans/16-content-target.md, authoring/RUNBOOK.md; follow-up task 464', 'Plan 70 design "Per-locale targets", "Translation aimed at gaps", "Source supply". No new target numbers: every launch language uses `targets.json` `base` (decision 21: Content target per player and language).

- `targets.deficits(pool, bundle, locale=None)`: with a locale, count that locale''s approved, non-stale translations (via `translations.py`) by their own difficulty.
- `qgen report --locale L` (default `es`) progress section; `target_check` of `--simulate` uses the same function (drop the "until part 9 sets per-locale targets" note).
