INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (623, 65, 'Start screen: supply warning (decision 31) and exhausted subcategories', 'work', 'done', 350, '2026-10-13, app/client/src/engine/outlook.ts (+test), game/SupplyNotice.svelte, game/Choice.svelte, game/Game.svelte, lib/api.ts, locales es/en/de, plans/decisions.md (D-82), plans/04, directory.md, plan 65 body', 'UI side of plan 65; replaces task 429 (dropped: its screens weren''t there). Needs the supply outlook (task 423, done), the mode screen (plan 36: task 378, task 379) and the configure screen (plan 59: task 391) done: the warning shows after mode, bundles and age group (or custom difficulty) are chosen, before level 1. If those screens are not there yet, stop and say so.

- Criterion (decision 31, replaces "k < K"; there is no K): warn only when a level the planned session needs (mode, bundles, age group / custom range, levels, cards) has 1 or 0 unseen questions left. `outlook()` (`app/client/src/engine/outlook.ts`) gives k, bottleneck, bundleHint, exhausted; add the tight check there (levels whose range can''t get ≥ 2 count-0 questions under the same Hall assignment, merged as difficulty ranges). Informational, «Jugar» stays.
- Texts in `app/client/src/locales/es.ts` (LUI-1, `npm run check:literals -w app/client`):
  - tight levels: e.g. «Casi no quedan preguntas nuevas de dificultad {lo}–{hi}; después se repetirán algunas.»
  - bundle hint: «Con el paquete {bundle} activado habría más.»
  - none left: «En esta partida pueden salir preguntas que ya vieron.»
  - exhausted: «Ya vieron todas las preguntas de: {list}», once per subcategory; call `noteExhausted` at every game start (it prunes) with the shown list.
- Reachable and dismissable with keys and pad (action layer, plan 44).
- Plan 65''s D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` and plan 65''s body: replace K / "pm decision 31" by decision 31''s rule.
- When done: `pm decision consequences 31 "<what changed>"` (the last task waiting for decision 31).

Checks: `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `check:literals`; in the browser (or desktop shell) with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` holding a crafted save: plenty left shows nothing, a level with ≤ 1 unseen shows the warning with the right range, none left the repeat line, an exhausted subcategory once and not on the next start. Never write `state/`.', '2026-10-13T00:44:11Z', '2026-10-13T05:07:59Z', 429);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (624, 46, 'Player: focus the name field on mount when there are no players', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/game/Player.svelte. Cause was not only the missing tick: go() keeps busy true through the fade-in, so the input was disabled when focus() ran. Fix: an $effect focuses the field once when loaded && !busy and there are no players (replaces the onMount focus). Checked in headless Chrome on a fresh TRIVIA_STATE: keyboard → field focused after Start, typing and Enter as before, no picker/Escribir; stubbed pad → A on Start lands on the field, next A opens the letter picker. npm run check/test/build, qgen validate pass.', 'Found by task 230. `app/client/src/game/Player.svelte` `onMount`: `loaded = true; if (players.length === 0) input?.focus();` runs before the `{#if loaded}` form renders, so `input` is still undefined and nothing gets focus (checked in Chromium: `document.activeElement` stays `body` on a fresh save). Plan 04 "Player" and plan 46 assume the field is focused on mount; with a pad the family must now press ↓ before A opens the letter picker.
- Fix: `await tick()` (svelte) between `loaded = true` and the focus.
- Check: `npm run check`; fresh save (`TRIVIA_STATE` temp dir), Start → Player: the field has focus; a pad A opens the letter picker directly; typing with the keyboard works as before.', '2026-10-13T01:07:39Z', '2026-10-13T01:12:37Z', 230);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (625, 59, 'Merge «Reportar pregunta» into the flag: dialog with optional note', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/src/game/FlagDialog.svelte (new), FlagList.svelte (was Reports.svelte), Game.svelte, Overlay.svelte, LetterPicker.svelte, letters.ts, engine/save.ts (v4 upgrade, setFlag with note), state.ts, game.ts/api.ts (report action gone), lib/api.ts, lib/types.ts, locales es/es-ES/en/de/xx (flag.*, picker.letters/marks; report.* and note_invalid dropped), app/server/save.py, authoring/tools/save_file.py, authoring/server/main.py, README, directory.md, plans 04/05/12/13. Headless Chrome walk: keyboard + mouse flag/edit/unflag, v2 report migrated, list with notes; real pad not walked (letter picker in note mode untested on a pad).', 'Gamemaster decision after the D25 play-test (see `pm decision list --answered --grep flag`): keep only the flag, give it the report''s dialog.

- Flag icon click and `flag.key` (M in es) open a dialog like the report confirm: title, optional free-text note, Enter flags, Esc/⌫ cancels; flagging an already flagged question: offer unflag or edit the note
- Note entry must work by keyboard, pad (`LetterPicker.svelte`) and later the Steam Deck on-screen keyboard; empty note is fine
- Drop the overlay item «Reportar pregunta»; keep the list (rename to «Preguntas marcadas» or similar) with «Copiar» for players without authoring tools; the note shows in the list and in the copied text
- Save: one structure for flags and reports (migrate `reports` rows and `flags` into it, bump the save version); old saves keep their entries
- `trivia-authoring` (`apply_flags` in `authoring/server/main.py`): needs-work feedback includes the note: «Marcada en el juego (player, date): <note>»
- Catalog: es/en/de/xx leaves for the dialog; drop unused `report.*` leaves; `check:literals` passes
- Docs: README line on `M` (also says it marks «needs work» on the next `trivia-authoring` start), plans 04 and 13 (MD-6, GM-5)', '2026-10-13T02:50:43Z', '2026-10-13T03:45:14Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (626, 82, 'Vite native config loader warning: import extensions in config files', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/credits.ts: .ts extension on the types import; vite.config.ts of app/client and authoring/ui have no other extensionless relative imports; npm run build prints no configLoader warning', 'Gamemaster saw on `npm run build -w app/client` (2026-10-13):

