INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (629, 69, 'Question content gets the question language as lang attribute', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/lib/names.svelte.ts (questionLocale(): locale of the engine data the last action ran on, i.e. the running game''s locale, which a game keeps (plan 68), else the save''s language.questions; xx UI stays es), lang={questionLocale()} on Question.svelte (question h1, hint notes, answers), Game.svelte (select card descriptions, correct/victory panels, wrong answer + fun fact), CategoryPicker.svelte (subcategory/category names), Shredder.svelte (purged subcategory name); theme.css: hyphens: auto also on [lang]:lang(de), hyphens: manual on other [lang] inside .game (decision 61); directory.md. Check: Playwright, de UI + es questions: select cards, question, answers, result panel lang=es, hyphens manual, main.game auto; es identical by construction (same lang, manual = default); de questions untested (no playable de pool). npm run check, test, build, qgen validate pass.', 'Question content carries the question language as its `lang` attribute, not the UI''s.

- Today `<html lang>` is the UI language (plan 68, `lib/i18n.ts`); question, answer, hint, explanation and select-card texts inherit it. With a German UI and Spanish questions, `.game:lang(de) { hyphens: auto }` (task 456, decision 61) hyphenates Spanish card text by German rules (seen: «pro-blema», «im-portante» on the select cards); screen readers get the wrong language too.
- Set `lang={questionLocale}` on the wrappers of question content: select cards (`Game.svelte` select screen), `Question.svelte` (text, answers, hints), result/wrong/victory explanation, category and bundle names if they come from the question locale''s names file. Question locale: the save''s `language.questions` (`fetchLanguage`/engine), not `lang` from `i18n.ts`.
- `xx` UI: question content stays `es`.
- Check: `?lang=de` with question language `es`: no hyphenation in Spanish card text; with `de` questions (once a de pool is playable) German hyphenation on long compounds. `es` pixel-identical (decision 6 method). `npm run check`, `npm run build`.', '2026-10-13T04:31:59Z', '2026-10-13T04:42:21Z', 456);
