INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (645, 85, 'Steam binding spike and bridge (steamworks-ffi-node)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/{package.json,package-lock.json,main.mjs,preload.cjs}, app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts, flake.nix, .gitignore; steamworks-ffi-node 0.11.3; under Steam (480): available true, SteamID and ''english'' logged and returned to the page; no SDK lib / bad App ID: available false, one stderr line; D-69 records the dev SDK source', 'Plan 85 task 1. Wire steamworks-ffi-node (decision 28: Steam binding for the Electron shell) into the Electron main process and expose one optional bridge to the page.

- `app/desktop/package.json`: `steamworks-ffi-node` pinned in `dependencies`, nothing else new.
- SDK libs: gitignore `app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/`; `setSdkPath` to it. Dev on NixOS: add nixpkgs `steamworks-sdk-redist` (unfree) to the flake dev shell and point the path there when the folder is missing (decision 68: Steamworks SDK downloaded for the Steam binding?).
- `main.mjs`: `STEAM_APP_ID = 480` (Spacewar) until part 1 answers the App ID; `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID` overrides in dev; the client''s `SteamAppId` env wins under a Steam launch. `init` in try/catch: any failure → `available: false`, one stderr line, nothing on screen. No `restartAppIfNecessary`, no DRM, `webRequest` block stays. `runCallbacks` on a timer only while Steam is up; stop on quit; `shutdown()` in `will-quit`.
- IPC channels `steam:*` with the same sender-origin check as `save:*`; `preload.cjs` adds `window.trivia.steam`; `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts` exports `steam: SteamBridge | null` with the full shape of plan 85 "Bridge" (`available`, `steamId()`, `language()`, `overlay`, `showTextInput(rect, current)`, `inputTypes()`, `setPresence(key, values)`, `unlock(id)`); this task implements `available`, `steamId()`, `language()` (`GetCurrentGameLanguage`), `unlock()` as plain pass-throughs; the rest are stubs returning false/null that later tasks fill.
- No Node/FFI in the page.

Done when: under a running Steam client with 480, `trivia-desktop` logs `available` true, SteamID and language; without Steam a full game plays and the D-72 save is untouched; browser game (`trivia`) unchanged; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-13T05:18:17Z', '2026-10-13T05:27:08Z', 644);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (646, 85, 'Steam language as the first-start guess', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/src/lib/engine.ts: async guessTag() asks steam.language() when available (rejection → navigator), STEAM_LANGS map (latam es, spanish es-ES, english en, german de, schinese zh-Hans, russian ru, brazilian pt-BR; unknown → navigator.language); only fresh saves (save.language wins). Checked defaultLanguage: de→de/de, es-ES→es-ES/es, es→es/es. No test (trivial table).', 'Plan 85 task 2 (milestone 10 outcome). Needs the bridge of task 1 (`steam.language()`).

- `guessTag()` in `app/client/src/lib/engine.ts` becomes `async` (only `ready()` calls it): `steam?.available ? fromSteam(await steam.language()) : null` ?? `navigator.language` ?? `es`.
- Pure mapping (in `lib/engine.ts` or a small `lib/steamlang.ts`): `latam` → `es`, `spanish` → `es-ES` (decision 27: Spanish variety; questions `es` via `defaultLanguage()`''s language-part match in `engine/save.ts`), `english` → `en`, `german` → `de`, `schinese` → `zh-Hans`, `russian` → `ru`, `brazilian` → `pt-BR` (fall through best match until milestone 12''s locales exist); unknown → `null`.
- Only the fresh-save preselection: `save.language` always wins; the first-start screen still asks (D-86).
- One small `node:test` for the mapping only if it stays useful.

Done when: fresh save with Steam language `german` preselects de/de, `spanish` es-ES/es, `latam` es/es, unknown → navigator; existing save unchanged; without Steam behaviour as before. Local CI passes.', '2026-10-13T05:18:18Z', '2026-10-13T05:28:05Z', 644);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (647, 85, 'Steam overlay spike and wiring', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/main.mjs, plans/decisions.md: Linux spike (XWayland, Intel Mesa, Electron 43.7.7, Steam 480): frame subscription before load gets no frames; with the native GL window attached the main process freezes; preloaded gameoverlayrenderer kills Electron outside a Steam launch → overlay Windows only (addElectronSteamOverlay after did-finish-load, Steam up only), Linux unchanged; overlay.enabled() = attached && IsOverlayEnabled; D-92, decision 70; Windows check folded into task 652''s gamemaster decision (needs task 650''s build)', 'Plan 85 task 3. steamworks-ffi-node''s overlay is experimental (offscreen render into a native OpenGL window; X11 only, ~1 frame latency, untested with `<video>`/`<audio>`).

- Spike on Linux X11 and Windows (the Deck/gamescope goes into masterplan 10 part 10''s checklist): overlay opens with Shift+Tab, video and audio questions play, frame rate fine, fullscreen/F11 still work.
- If OSR breaks video/audio: overlay on Windows only, Linux without overlay; Deck runs the Windows build via Proton (D-63, SW-12).
- Wire the chosen path in `main.mjs` behind `steam.available`; fill the bridge''s `overlay` part. The game pauses nothing on overlay open.
- Record the result: `pm decision record "Steam overlay in the Electron shell" …` and a D-entry in `plans/decisions.md`.
- Where a real Steam session on a machine the worker can''t drive is needed, ask the gamemaster with `pm decision add` (concrete steps, expected result) and make this task pending on it.

Done when: overlay result recorded; chosen path wired; without Steam nothing changes. Local CI passes.', '2026-10-13T05:18:18Z', '2026-10-13T05:40:11Z', 644);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (648, 85, 'Steam on-screen keyboard for the player name', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/main.mjs, app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts, app/client/src/game/Player.svelte, plans/14-input.md: steam:show-text-input opens ShowFloatingGamepadTextInput (SingleLine) at the field''s rect in device pixels, only in Big Picture or on the Deck, else false → LetterPicker; A on the field and «Escribir» try Steam first; no new strings. Big Picture/Deck check folded into task 652''s gamemaster decision (body updated with steps and the ShowGamepadTextInput fallback follow-up).', 'Plan 85 task 4. Player screen name field under Steam with a pad.

- Bridge `showTextInput(rect, current) → Promise<boolean>`: `ShowFloatingGamepadTextInput` at the field''s rect (keystrokes into the focused `<input>`); false outside Big Picture/Deck → `LetterPicker.svelte` (plan 46) as today.
- If keystrokes don''t reach Chromium: `ShowGamepadTextInput` + `GetEnteredGamepadTextInput` (returns the text, the page sets the field) instead; note which in `plans/14-input.md`.
- Keyboard/mouse users keep the plain field; the picker stays the fallback without Steam.
- New strings via `t()` in every catalog (es, es-ES where it differs, en, de); `check:literals` passes.

Done when: under Big Picture/Deck the keyboard fills the name (gamemaster check via `pm decision add` if the worker can''t run it); elsewhere the picker as before. Local CI passes.', '2026-10-13T05:18:18Z', '2026-10-13T05:41:39Z', 644);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (649, 85, 'Pad glyphs from Steam Input types', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/main.mjs (Steam Input init, steam:input-types), app/client/src/lib/gamepad.ts (steamStyle), gamepad.svelte.ts, plans/14-input.md; real-Steam check added to task 652', 'Plan 85 task 5. With Steam Input on, every pad is a virtual Xbox pad, so `styleOf(Gamepad.id)` in `app/client/src/lib/gamepad.ts` says Xbox.

- Steam Input init in main; bridge `inputTypes() → PadStyle[] | null` = `GetInputTypeForHandle` of the connected handles.
- One PlayStation-type pad → `playstation` glyphs (`Glyph.svelte`); Steam Deck / Steam Controller / others → Xbox (no Deck glyph set without a pm decision); mixed types → Xbox (per-player glyphs come with IN-6). `null` or no Steam → `Gamepad.id` as today.
