INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (666, 88, 'Store texts per language in 17a (LUI-6)', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 88 task 1. Free DLC texts are `task 783` (same plan).

- `plans/17a-store-page.md` exists (requirements, screenshots; listed in `plans/README.md`): add per store language a block with every field and its Steam character limit (check Steamworks docs today, cite): English (`en`) first, then `es` (es-419), `es-ES` (only fields that differ: vosotros, regionalisms), `de`, before the existing sections; leave a section "Free DLC" for `task 783`. README row status: drop "stub" once texts are in.
- Fields: store name (D-50: «Living Room Trivia», «Trivia en Familia»; de «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» per decision 78: German store name, pending PUB-7''s check in `task 253`''s plan: mark it provisional in 17a), short description (≤ 300 chars), "About this game" long description, feature bullets (12 in a row, the five modes per D-74, jokers by their localized names, offline, gamepad/keyboard, family on the TV, Steam Cloud saves per Steam account (plan 87), Steam achievements (plan 86; only uncustomized games earn them, decision 19)), privacy line, controller line.
- Wording from the in-game catalogs `app/client/src/locales/*.ts` (mode names, joker names: de per decisions 54–58).
- Steam only (decision 111): no text about running without Steam; where saves come up, say plainly that saves need Steam (a Steam account).
- Privacy line: collects nothing, sends nothing; player names stay on the device and in Steam Cloud (plan 87). Controller line: no "full controller support" claim; decision 90: ''Partial'' until the pad-only run passes.
- Leave placeholder sections for the AI disclosure (`task 667`), capsules and icon (`task 669`), screenshots and trailer, entry checklist (`task 672`); requirements/languages/controller already exist (`task 668`).
- Approval: one `pm decision add "Store texts approved? (<lang>)"` per language set (en, es + es-ES, de), body = path + section; mention a native-speaker read where LUI-5''s testers (plan 69) are available. Answers with fixes: apply them in a follow-up task (`pm task add 88 …`) or before closing if they arrive in time.

Done when: 17a has the four blocks, approval decisions added. LUI-6 `[x]` in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` once approved (else `task 672` does it).', '2026-10-13T06:07:02Z', NULL, 665);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (667, 88, 'AI disclosure text (Steam survey + store wording)', 'work', 'open', 240, NULL, 'Plan 88 task 3. Needs PUB-10''s line (Anthropic commercial-use terms) in `plans/17-publishing.md`, from part 1 of masterplan 10 (`task 253` and the plan it writes). Missing → find the pending decision or task that blocks it, `pm task-pending-decision` on that decision (or add one: "PUB-10 line in plan 17?") and stop.

- Check Valve''s current AI disclosure rules (Steamworks content survey "AI Generated Content": pre-generated vs live-generated; whether dev tools such as code assistants count; whether each free DLC app (decision 66) needs its own disclosure); cite the page and date in 17a.
- Draft in `plans/17a-store-page.md`: survey answer ("pre-generated" description; "live-generated": none) and the store-page wording per language (en, es, es-ES if different, de); for the free DLC (`colombia`, es + en, decision 110) a line in its languages if Valve asks for one.
- Facts:
  - pre-generated: LLM-drafted questions (Claude drafts, fact-checks with web search, reviews: D-7, D-10, D-32/D-33, `reviewer: "llm"`; translates: D-87); a person checks, edits and approves (gamemaster review, independent LLM audit + blind human spot check per batch D-56, native-speaker playtests LUI-5)
  - LLM-written code (the game''s code is written with Claude)
  - live-generated: none: nothing is generated while you play
  - no AI-generated art, images, sound or music: people''s work from Wikimedia Commons and other free sources, credited in CREDITS.md
  - store art typographic (decision 77: Store capsule art): template in code, AI-assisted if Claude designed it (`task 669` says whether)
- Steam only (decision 111): no wording about running without Steam.
- Anything unclear in Valve''s rules → in the approval decision''s body.
- Approval: `pm decision add "AI disclosure approved?"` (the gamemaster approves the wording). Entry is part 9''s (PUB-9, `task 259`), not this task''s.

Done when: draft in 17a, approval decision added.', '2026-10-13T06:07:03Z', NULL, 665);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (668, 88, 'System requirements, supported languages, controller flags', 'work', 'done', 170, '2026-10-13, plans/17a-store-page.md (requirements per OS, languages table, controller flags; depots measured from the local --dir build: 2.95 GB installed); decision 90 for the gamemaster (incl. real-pad run); follow-up task 688 (apply answer, storage after media bundle) pending on it', 'Plan 88 task 3. Needs part 7''s first packaged builds (`task 261: write plan: Builds, depots and upload` and its plan) and part 6''s media bundle (`task 260`). If they aren''t built yet: `pm task-pending-decision` on the decision that blocks their open tasks (`pm show` them) and stop; if none blocks: `pm decision add "Packaged builds ready for the store requirements?"`, pend on it and stop.

- In `plans/17a-store-page.md`, minimum/recommended per OS: Windows 10/11 x64; SteamOS / Linux x64 (distro the Linux build was tested on); CPU, RAM, GPU from what plays smoothly on the test machines (ask the gamemaster in a decision if unknown); disk = installed size of the depots (today''s plan 56 builds ~2.5 GB each only as a placeholder).
- Supported-languages table: interface + subtitles ✓ for English, Spanish – Latin America, Spanish – Spain, German; full audio ✗.
- Controller flags: "full controller support" only if a pad-only game passes start to victory incl. a new player (name entry: plan 46 letter picker, SW-8 floating keyboard, plan 85); else "partial". PlayStation/Xbox glyph flags per plan 45. Deck compatibility is part 10''s (`task 262`), not this task''s.
- Gamemaster check: `pm decision add` with the values (pad-only run result included); options approve / fix.

Done when: values in 17a, decision added.', '2026-10-13T06:07:03Z', '2026-10-13T08:23:16Z', 665);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (669, 88, 'Capsules, logo and icon: render per store language', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 88 task 5. Decision 77: Store capsule art: typographic template in code, «Trivia» wordmark in the game''s fonts (Baloo 2, Nunito) and colours, rendered per size and language by a script; AI-assisted if Claude designs it. Decision 87: Windows exe icon: the same script renders a 1024×1024 icon (`task 683` waits for it). Capsules aren''t screenshots of the UI: they render now, not late (decision 79''s timing is for screenshots and trailer).

- Valve''s current graphical-asset list, checked today and cited in `plans/17a-store-page.md` (2024 reference: header 920×430, small 462×174, main 1232×706, vertical 748×896, page background 1438×810, library capsule 600×900, library hero 3840×1240, library logo 1280×720 PNG, library header 920×430, community icon 184×184; recheck sizes and text-area/safe-zone rules). Also Valve''s DLC asset list (which capsules a DLC store page needs).
- Localized per store language (D-50; `es` and `es-ES` share; de «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» per decision 78, provisional until PUB-7''s check).
- Each free DLC (decision 66; decision 110: `colombia`, es + en): its capsules in its languages only, pack name from the DLC texts in 17a (`task 783`; else the in-game name from `app/data/bundles.json`), recognisably the same family as the base capsules.
- Icon: square 1024×1024 PNG, legible at 16×16 (derived from the community icon), output path stable so `task 683` can set `win.icon` / Linux / Steam client icon from it.
- Script `authoring/store/capsules.mjs`, output `authoring/store/out/capsules/` (gitignored; per DLC `out/capsules/dlc-<id>/`, icon `out/capsules/icon-1024.png` or similar); no new npm dependency (raw CDP via Node''s `WebSocket` against the shell''s `--remote-debugging-port` as `screenshots.mjs` does, or Electron `capturePage` behind a dev-only flag). Template in the game''s palette (`plans/10-visual-design.md`), «Trivia» as the main element.
- Credit/disclose as decision 77 says (CREDITS.md / `app/client/credits.ts`; note in 17a''s AI section for `task 667`).
- `directory.md`: the script and output folder.
- Approval: `pm decision add "Capsules and icon approved?"` with the output paths (base, DLC, icon); fixes → follow-up task. After approval tell `task 683` (its decision 87 answer points here) where the icon is, if its body doesn''t say.

Done when: every asset per language rendered, base and each free DLC, plus the icon; approval decision added.', '2026-10-13T06:07:03Z', NULL, 665);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (670, 88, 'Scripted store screenshots at 1920×1080', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/store/screenshots.mjs, plans/17a-store-page.md (new: Screenshots), plans/README.md, directory.md, .gitignore (authoring/store/out/), flake.nix (xvfb in the dev shell); 30 PNGs rendered offline from the dev shell (es, es-ES 10 each; en, de 5: no pools); decision 79 → gamemaster; follow-up task 673 (en/de re-run); check, test, build, qgen validate pass', 'Plan 88 task 5.

- `authoring/store/screenshots.mjs`: starts the shell (`trivia-desktop`) at 1920×1080 with a throw-away demo save (made-up player names, no family data) in `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` (temp dir, deleted after); per UI language (en, es, es-ES if the UI differs, de) walks a fixed set of screens: start, an image question, an audio/video question, a joker in action, the tower near level 12, victory, mode choice; writes PNGs to `authoring/store/out/screenshots/<lang>/` (gitignored). ≥ 5 per language (Valve minimum).
- No new npm dependency: Node''s built-in `WebSocket` + raw CDP against `--remote-debugging-port` (as task 318 did), or Electron `capturePage` behind a dev-only flag. Drive the game through the UI or seed the save; media from the cache (`trivia-media sync --status approved` first).
- A language without enough approved questions in `app/data/pool.json` yet: render what exists, add a follow-up task (`pm task add 88 …`) to re-run it once its content lands.
- `directory.md`: the script and output folder; a line in 17a on how to re-run (after visual changes).
- Approval: `pm decision add "Store screenshots: which set?"` with the paths; the gamemaster picks.

Done when: script runs offline from the dev shell, PNGs per language, decision added.', '2026-10-13T06:07:04Z', '2026-10-13T06:21:17Z', 665);
