INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (895, 110, 'Release check: telemetry row', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 110 task 2 (read "Decisions taken here" in the plan body). Needs plans 106–109 done and task 870: Release check: report row, report step, Steam offline row closed; if one isn''t, leave this task as it is.

- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: new `MANUAL["telemetry"]`, `full` only (like plan 104''s `report` row: a content-only patch ships no client or shell code; the server deploys apart from builds). No automated step: the `report` step already checks the base URL''s `/health`, the only shared dependency. Row text: `beta` under Steam, online: answer «Sí» (or Esc menu on), play one game, quit → `qgen telemetry --pull` folds ≥ 1 session from that version, `qgen report --played` lists it in its session stats; switch off, play, quit → main log `trivia: telemetry off`, no `telemetry →` line, the next pull folds 0. Check the log lines and commands against plans 107/109 as built.
- `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)": rows table (`telemetry` row), Patch variant (one bullet: why full only), decision template example (row added), `failed` routing: server (404/500 on `/telemetry`, pull/ack, retention) → plan 105; nothing recorded, wrong fields → plan 106; no request, a request when opted out, close delayed > 4 s, a visible error → plan 107; consent screen/Esc row/texts → plan 108; pull or report wrong → plan 109; closed plan: a new task in it anyway, several hit: a new plan in milestone 14.
- Check: a `--manual` file answering every row incl. `telemetry` parses; a run with every step skipped lists the new row; a content-only run shows it as skipped. Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).

Done when: `trivia-release-check` has the `telemetry` row (full only) and ST-4 documents it with its routing.', '2026-10-13T17:43:24Z', NULL, 883);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (896, 110, 'Gamemaster: telemetry end-to-end on beta under Steam', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 110 task 3. Needs task 894: Gamemaster: deploy telemetry and publish the store text (decision answered, server deployed) and task 895: Release check: telemetry row done; if not, leave this task as it is. Workers never log in, deploy or upload.

- Prepare the tag/version notes (version to bump, `v<version>` tag, what''s in the build: plans 106–108) for the gamemaster.
- `pm decision add` (kind once) "Telemetry: end-to-end check on beta", rows with exact steps (gamemaster uploads with `trivia-steam upload --branch beta` and plays; check every path, log line and command against the code as built):
  - fresh install (or `<userData>/telemetry/install.json` deleted): consent asked once after the language screen, «No» focused; pad, keyboard, mouse.
  - opted out: one game, quit → no session on the server (`qgen telemetry --pull --dry-run` empty), main log `telemetry off`.
  - opted in: two games (one won, one lost; jokers used), quit via «Salir» → `qgen telemetry --pull` folds them; `qgen report --played` shows played vs. rated difficulty rows and session stats (outliers only with enough samples; a seeded dev run already showed that list, plan 109).
  - closes (plan 107, decision 120: Telemetry send: at quit, one later try at the next start): Steam "Stop" on Linux/Deck → session arrives at quit or next start; Windows Steam "Stop" → next start (≈ 30 s after load); Deck sleep → resume → quit → arrives; network off at quit → arrives on the next online start; close never delayed noticeably, no error shown.
  - switch off in the Esc menu → `<userData>/telemetry/` holds no session and no install id.
  - store privacy text live with this build''s release (before `beta` goes to the default branch).
  - Answer = date + ✓/✗ per row.
- `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <decision>` and stop.
- After the answer: ✗ → follow-up tasks per the plan''s `failed` routing; `pm decision consequences` on the decision; note in the body of task 897: Close-out docs (telemetry) (`pm task set … --body`) whether milestone 14''s "Done when" is met and the Steam close behaviour found. Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).

Done when: the decision is answered, ✗ rows have follow-up tasks, the close-out task has the findings.', '2026-10-13T17:43:24Z', NULL, 883);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (897, 110, 'Close-out docs (telemetry)', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 110 task 4. Needs task 896: Gamemaster: telemetry end-to-end on beta under Steam done (its findings are added to this body); if not, leave this task as it is.

- `plans/11-steam.md`: principle 3 → "Offline, no accounts; opt-in telemetry only (milestone 14)": the game works without network, sends nothing without a stored yes; ST-5''s "(no telemetry, so by hand …)" → reports via plan 103''s server, opt-in telemetry see milestone 14 (plans 105–109); ST-5 note with deploy date and retention (30 days, decision 118: Telemetry server storage and pull token).
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md`: shell section: telemetry store and IPC (`telemetry:state|consent|load|record`), send at quit + one try at next start (decision 120: Telemetry send: at quit, one later try at the next start), ticket identity `trivia-telemetry` next to `trivia-reports`, per-install consent (decision 121: Telemetry consent: stored per install, not in the save); Steam close behaviour as found in task 896.
- `directory.md`: `app/desktop/telemetry.mjs`, client `engine/telemetry.ts`/`lib/telemetry.ts`, `ConsentScreen.svelte`, `authoring/tools/played.py`, `state/played/`, `report-server/` telemetry files (only what plans 105–109 didn''t add; check real names).
- `README.md` "How to …": "Pull gameplay data and read the played difficulty" (`qgen telemetry --pull`, `qgen report --played`, `/review?played=outliers`, nothing changes without the gamemaster), "Test telemetry locally" (`trivia-report-server dev`, `seed-telemetry`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_REPORT_URL`, `TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR`), deploy line under the report-server how-to.
- `AGENTS.md` "Commands": `qgen telemetry --pull`, `qgen report --played`, `trivia-report-server seed-telemetry` if missing (`.md` style rules).
- `plans/project.md`: milestone 14 line `[x]` with date and pm plans 101, 105–110.
- `grep -rni "no telemetry\|never phones home"` over docs and code: none left.
- `pm decision consequences` on decisions 118–121 where the built result differs or adds facts; check milestone 14''s "Done when" and plan 101''s; a gap → follow-up task. Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).

Done when: no doc says "no telemetry" or "never phones home"; docs, how-tos and decision consequences match the built telemetry.', '2026-10-13T17:43:24Z', NULL, 883);
