INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (942, 104, 'Release check: mods step and Workshop row (milestone 15)', 'work', 'open', 160, NULL, 'Plan 102 part 12 (plan "Modding end-to-end check and close-out", milestone 15) decided that every release candidate checks mods: an automated step `mods` (always) and a manual row `workshop` (full only). This task adds both to `trivia-release-check`. Priority 160: it runs after milestone 15''s parts, which it needs.

Needs (stop and say so if not done; don''t close):
- task 870: Release check: report row, report step, Steam offline row; task 786: Smoke game under the dev switch (TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER)
- milestone 15''s plans 112 (overlay, `--no-mods`), 115 (bundles from mods), 117 (`window.trivia`, `/mods.js`), 118 (mods screen, notice, crash marker), 120 task 5 (`modkit` step: `--check-mod` on `modding/template-bundle`), 121 task 3 (examples shipped in `modding/examples/`, `modkit` covers them)

Work:
- `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs`: option `--mods`: a third run (after the existing ones), same clean env, network off, dev switch, temp `HOME`:
  - before the start: copy `<unpacked>/modding/template-bundle` and `<unpacked>/modding/examples/{theme,rules-tweak}` into the temp `HOME`''s `<userData>/mods/` (path as `main.mjs` resolves it under that `HOME`; not `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, so the packaged path is tested), and a `mods.json` with the notice accepted and the three on (format per plan 112/118, written as the shell writes it).
  - start: over CDP, `window.triviaShell.mods.list()` shows the three `loaded`, no error; a CSS variable the theme sets has the theme''s value (`getComputedStyle`); the player bundle is offered in the bundle selector marked player-made; a new player plays levels 1–3 with the player bundle on (the rules tweak''s extra Soplo shows in the joker count); after 20 s no `mods-start.json` (plan 118).
  - conversion: add `examples/conversion` on top (`mods.json`), restart: the conversion''s own element shows, our start screen doesn''t; restart with `--no-mods`: our start screen, `mods.list()` reports the flag safe start.
  - exit 1 names the step, as the other runs.
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: step `mods` after `smoke` (`node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --mods <UNPACKED>`), always (no content-only skip: data changes can break the merged `bundles.json`, decision 128); `MANUAL["workshop"]` (`full`): "beta under Steam with the example theme subscribed from the Workshop: the mods screen lists it as Workshop, loaded, the colours change; Steam launch options `--no-mods`: plain game, mods screen says why; remove the option"; docstring step list.
- `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)": How to run (the `mods` step), rows table (`workshop` row), Patch variant (one bullet: `mods` always because of the merge, `workshop` full only: Workshop discovery is shell code), decision template example rows, `failed` routing: `mods` step or `workshop` row ✗ → the plan of the code involved in milestone 15 (overlay plan 112, Workshop plan 114, bundles plan 115, add-ons plan 117, screen plan 118, examples plan 121), once closed a new plan in milestone 15.
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` SW-6 step list; `AGENTS.md` "Commands" `trivia-release-check` line (`mods` step).

Check: `trivia-desktop-build --dir`, then `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --mods app/desktop/release/linux-unpacked` passes; a throw-away break (e.g. a typo in a temp copy''s theme `style.css` selector, or a removed example) fails with the step named (don''t keep it); `trivia-release-check --skip tag --skip checks --skip licenses --skip quality --skip nix --skip manual` runs `mods` ✓; a `--manual` file answering every row incl. `workshop` parses; a content-only run lists `workshop` as "skipped: content-only since <tag>" and still runs `mods`. Per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T18:27:52Z', NULL, 910);
