INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (944, 111, 'Readable build config: preserveModules, decision 124 names, stable cssHash', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/vite.config.ts (minify off, sourcemaps, cssCodeSplit, modulePreload off, preserveModules + naming functions per decision 124: <path>.js, <path>.svelte.js, <path>.svelte.css, vendor/svelte/…, _virtual/_vite/preload-helper.js; trivia-one-entry-script plugin: dist/index.html loads only /main.js + /app.css), app/client/svelte.config.js (cssHash svelte-<path>, e.g. svelte-game-hud). dist: 170 JS (96 vendor/svelte), 32 CSS, 4.1 MB without audio/fonts; no hash, no node_modules/, no assets/. JS files without .map: 40 import-only vendor stubs (no code after tree-shaking) and _virtual/_vite/preload-helper.js. Played levels 1–3 (image, audio, video) on release/linux-unpacked with a throw-away smoke copy under TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1; the stock smoke.mjs fails at start (report.mjs, telemetry.mjs not packaged: task 1000, new task 1002) and its resume check fails on the old hashed build too (task 786 already lists it). Per-commit checks pass.', 'Plan 111 task 1. Make `npm run build` of `app/client` emit one unminified, unhashed file per source module with source maps, named per decision 124: Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides.

- `app/client/vite.config.ts` `build`: `minify: false`, `sourcemap: true`, `cssCodeSplit: true`; `modulePreload` off (or a small plugin) so `dist/index.html` loads only `<script type="module" src="/main.js">` and `app.css` (task 899''s test build got ~110 script tags + `_virtual/_vite/modulepreload-polyfill.js`).
- `rollupOptions.output`: `preserveModules: true`, `preserveModulesRoot: "src"`; `entryFileNames`/`chunkFileNames`/`assetFileNames` as functions (`[name]` drops `.svelte` and collides `App.svelte` with `app.css` → `App2.js`):
  - `src/<path>.ts` → `<path>.js`; `<path>.svelte` → `<path>.svelte.js`; `x.svelte.ts` → `x.svelte.js`
  - component CSS → `game/Game.svelte.css` (not `Game.svelte_svelte_type_style_lang.css`); global CSS keeps its path (`app.css`, `game/theme.css`)
  - `node_modules/<pkg>/<path>` → `vendor/<pkg>/<path>`; Vite helpers → `_virtual/…`
  - assets without hash; `public/` (`audio/`, `fonts/`) unchanged
- `app/client/svelte.config.js`: `compilerOptions.cssHash` from the component path (e.g. `svelte-game-hud`), unique per component, not per CSS content.
- Svelte `dev/*` modules shipped as files: fine, drop only if an option does it cheaply.
- Keep `define __APP_VERSION__`, `credits()` plugin, dev proxy. No new dependencies (decision 106).

Done when: `npm run build` gives the decision 124 layout (spot-check `game/Game.svelte.js`, `game/Game.svelte.css`, `lib/data.js`, `vendor/svelte/…`, `.map` next to each JS, no hashed file, no `node_modules/` and no `assets/` in `dist/`); `dist/index.html` has one module script; the game plays a few levels on the built client (in `trivia-desktop`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`); per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T18:28:36Z', '2026-10-13T21:04:57Z', 911);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (945, 111, 'Override by path: throw-away proof (component JS, component CSS, theme.css)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, nothing committed (throw-away). Used plan 112''s real overlay instead of a roots() edit: temp mod (mod.json + game/Hud.svelte.js, game/Hud.svelte.css, game/theme.css edited from a fresh build) via TRIVIA_MODS_DIR, dev shell under Xvfb (TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1, TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1, own --user-data-dir, temp TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR), CDP script: new player → solo → level 1 question screen. Without mod: HUD ''Nivel 1'', .level rgb(255,184,28), --night-900 #0b1120. With mod: ''MODDED Nivel 1'', rgb(255,0,255), #00ff00 (stage background green); question, media, jokers fine, no errors. Source maps: game/Hud.svelte.js.map and game/Game.svelte.js.map sources resolve to /src/game/Hud.svelte, /src/game/Game.svelte. Note: an overridden JS keeps our .map unless the mod ships its own (stale lines in devtools only). Temp dir deleted, state/desktop/mods.json restored.', 'Plan 111 task 2. Prove a mod can replace single files of the readable build (task 1) by path. Throw-away: nothing committed.

- Copy `app/client/dist/` to a temp dir; change one component''s JS (a visible text in `game/Hud.svelte.js`), one component CSS (e.g. `game/Hud.svelte.css`) and `game/theme.css` (a colour variable).
- Point the shell at the copy (temporary `roots()` edit in `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` or an env var, not committed) and start `trivia-desktop` (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`).
- Check: the three changes visible, the game otherwise plays; source maps resolve in devtools to `src/…`.

Done when: the three overrides show in the game; result in this task''s done note (plan 112 builds the real overlay). Revert temp edits, delete the temp dir.', '2026-10-13T18:28:36Z', '2026-10-13T21:10:23Z', 911);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (946, 111, 'No stale files across updates: cache-control and the two-build check', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/resolve.mjs (cache-control: no-cache for client and mod-overlay files), plans/18-steam-integration.md (Builds and depots: stale client files finding). Check: fresh --user-data-dir, stamps appended to built main.js and game/Game.svelte.js, CDP read per start; A,A,B,C without the header and D,D,E,F with it: every start ran the current bytes. HTTP cache held no app:// entry (only a spellcheck .bdic: follow-up task 1003); no ses.clearCache() needed. Per-commit checks pass.', 'Plan 111 task 3. Without hashes, a cached old module could mix with new ones after an update.

- `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` `sendFile`: add `cache-control: no-cache` for `dist` (client) responses; media/data unchanged unless the check says otherwise.
- Check: build A, start `trivia-desktop`, rebuild with a visibly changed module, start again: the new code runs. Try with and without the header if needed to learn whether Chromium caches `app://` (`protocol.handle`) responses at all; also V8''s code cache (should invalidate on changed bytes). The session lives in `userData` across runs.
- Only if stale code shows despite the header: clear the session cache at start (`ses.clearCache()`) when the build id changed (`__APP_VERSION__` from `app/desktop/package.json`, decision 91/92, plus a build stamp written by `vite.config.ts`), stamp stored in `userData`. No version-keyed URLs (they break override paths).

Done when: the two-build check passes; the finding (cached or not) is one line in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T18:28:37Z', '2026-10-13T21:15:28Z', 911);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (947, 111, 'Readable build: packaging, credits, smoke and dev server checks', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/electron-builder.yml. trivia-desktop-build --dir: resources/client/ in win- and linux-unpacked identical to app/client/dist (380 files, all 153 vendor/ and 130 .map survive extraResources, no filter change). Fixed: report.mjs and telemetry.mjs (tasks 699/859) were missing from files: the packaged shell crashed at start (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND). credits_check both builds ok unchanged (Svelte credited once). trivia-steam stage ok (607 files per OS depot; stage has no --dry-run). smoke.mjs fails as task 786 says (save/local, resume selector); a throw-away copy with TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1, save/dev and the level selector fixed passed both runs (with and without packs) on the readable build. Size per OS depot: client code 2.23 MB (JS+CSS 0.84 MB, maps 1.39 MB) vs ~0.34 MB hashed: +~1.9 MB. task 762 body: vite preview must serve the readable tree.', 'Plan 111 task 4. Check the readable client build (task 1) through the release tooling.

- `trivia-desktop-build --dir`: `resources/client/` in `{win,linux}-unpacked/` has the readable tree; all `vendor/` and `.map` files survive electron-builder''s filters (`app/desktop/electron-builder.yml` `extraResources`), else fix the filter.
- `authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs` and the `credits` plugin (`app/client/credits.ts`) pass unchanged: Svelte, now under `vendor/svelte/`, still credited once (MIT, licence text in `CREDITS.md`).
- `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` both runs (with and without packs) pass; `trivia-steam stage --dry-run` (or `trivia-release-check --skip tag …` for the desktop builds, credits, smoke steps) passes.
- Plan 99 (`Retire the browser game and the Python game server`) isn''t done: add a line to its open `task 762: Node dev server for browser checks` (`pm task set 762 --body …`, keep its text) that its built-client command (`vite preview`) must serve the readable tree; `vite` dev is unaffected. If 762 is done by then, check `vite preview` directly.

Done when: those commands pass; build size per depot noted in the done note (expected + ~2 MB).', '2026-10-13T18:28:37Z', '2026-10-13T21:49:07Z', 911);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task) VALUES (948, 111, 'Start time on the Steam Deck: gamemaster check (decision once)', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 111 task 5. ~200 module requests over `app://` instead of 3 may slow the start. Runs after task 944 (readable build config); doesn''t block the other tasks.

- Raise `pm decision add "Readable build: start time on the Steam Deck ok?"` (kind once), body with the steps: install the beta build with the readable client (or, only if no beta upload is due, copy the unpacked Windows build to the Deck as a non-Steam test), time launch → start menu three times, compare with the previous (hashed) build; also on the gamemaster''s PC. Budget ≤ +0.5 s on the Deck.
- Options: "ok (≤ +0.5 s)" (recommended) | "too slow: bundle the Svelte runtime" (one `vendor/svelte.js`, ours still per module) | "too slow: other".
- Note decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand — the gamemaster may have no Deck; say so in the body (PC timing then, Deck later).
- Make this task pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`), stage, stop. On answer: "too slow" → add a follow-up task in plan 111 with the chosen fix.

Done when: the decision is answered and any follow-up added.', '2026-10-13T18:28:49Z', NULL, 911);
