INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (33, 'Configure game screen: which fields?', 'answered', '["as proposed in plan 13 (age group, bundles, joker set, media on/off, start level)", "shorter: age group, bundles, joker set only"]', 'Gamemaster mode (MD-11) gets a configure screen before every game: plan 29''s Choice screen, opening on the last choice, so Enter straight through = today''s game. Proposal in plans/13-game-modes.md "Proposal A": age group, bundles, joker set (Sin límite / Como las cartas / Estándar / A medida), media questions on/off, start level. Trade-off: media on/off and start level are new engine settings (selection filter, start state) and shrink supply or shorten games; the shorter list needs nothing beyond plan 29 + today''s budget.', 'Configure screen fields (opens on the last choice):
- Difficulty: pick an age group, or «Custom»: start and end difficulty (1–15), end >= start; levels ramp evenly from start to end.
- Bundles: a reusable bundle selector (used elsewhere too): every bundle available in the current language, base bundles shown apart from the others. Exactly one base bundle per game (D38). Default: the locale''s first base bundle; non-base bundles off.
- Jokers: one row per joker, a number or ∞; default = the standard set (STANDARD_JOKERS). No presets (no Sin límite / Como las cartas / Estándar picker).
- Allow video questions on/off, allow audio questions on/off; both default on. No general media on/off.
- Number of levels: 1–20, default 12; the Tower adapts. Replaces start level.
- Cards to choose from per level (by description): 0–4, default 4; 0 skips the choice and shows a question directly.', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:12:49Z', '2026-10-12T22:05:48Z', 389, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 390: 2026-10-12, task 390: D-88; plan 13 ''Configure game screen'' spec: new optional settings difficulty {start,end}, video/audio (false only), levels (missing 12), cards (missing 4); fresh defaults (standard set, first base bundle only) apply on the configure screen only; games without the fields and new without jokers play as before (fixtures unchanged); LEVELS/PER_LEVEL become per game.

2026-10-12, task 497: 2026-10-12, task 497: engine: Choice = every configure field (age_group | difficulty, bundles, levels, cards, video, audio, jokers); rangesFor (decision 46), cards 0 opens at once, media filter, choice/new/outlook take CHOICE_KEYS; fresh player''s choice: first base bundle + STANDARD_JOKERS

2026-10-13, task 391: Task 391 (2026-10-12): Choice.svelte in gamemaster mode is the configure game screen: Difficulty (age groups, then «A medida» with Desde/Hasta 1–15), Niveles 1–20, Cartas por nivel 0–4, video/audio switches, one stepper per joker 0–99 or ∞ (wrapping), and the new shared game/BundleSelector.svelte (base radio group apart from the toggles). Preset = playerChoice (every field of the newest game), fresh player = young_teens, first base bundle only, STANDARD_JOKERS, video/audio on, 12 levels, 4 cards; new always gets every field. The old per-tile age-group and bundle rows remain only in «Solo o en grupo» (age group). Strings configure.* (es, en, de). Backspace/B goes back, Esc stays the overlay. Outlook display left to task 623.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (34, 'Gamemaster menu: which cheats?', 'answered', '["as proposed in plan 13 (kept items, Gestionar comodines, Cambiar pregunta, Saltar a nivel, age group / bundles mid-game)", "shorter: kept items, Gestionar comodines, Cambiar pregunta only"]', 'The Esc overlay becomes the gamemaster menu (MD-12). Proposal in plans/13-game-modes.md "Proposal B": today''s items kept; joker budget becomes «Gestionar comodines» (give back / take away uses left); new «Cambiar pregunta» (same level and subcategory, not seen by default); «Saltar a nivel»; age group / bundles mid-game. Not proposed: reveal the answer (the family sees the TV). Trade-off: each new cheat is an engine action plus a menu row and a test; jump to level and mid-game settings are rarely needed, undo and skip already cover most mishaps.', 'As proposed in plan 13 (option 1), menu split in two parts:
- General (every mode): continue, «Reportar pregunta» / «Preguntas reportadas», sound, fullscreen, restart, quit (desktop).
- Gamemaster cheats (gamemaster mode only, kept apart from the general part): «Saltar pregunta», «Bloquear pregunta», undo, «Gestionar comodines», «Cambiar pregunta», «Saltar a nivel» (1..number of levels, D33), difficulty (age group or Custom, D33) and bundles (shared bundle selector, D33) mid-game.
- Not: reveal the answer.', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:12:50Z', '2026-10-12T22:08:39Z', 389, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 390: 2026-10-12, task 390: D-88; plan 13 ''Gamemaster menu'' spec: general part (every mode) vs cheats (gamemaster only, gamemaster_only 409); new engine actions replace {seen?} (outcome admin_replace), level {level}, settings {age_group|difficulty, bundles}; Gestionar comodines edits uses left over the existing jokers action; MD-10 [x], the menu''s new editors need focus/scope work (noted under MD-12).

2026-10-13, task 392: 2026-10-13, task 392: Overlay.svelte is the gamemaster menu: general column (continue, «Preguntas marcadas», fullscreen, credits, restart = abandon + the player''s configure screen, quit; sound, languages) and a dashed panel «Trucos del anfitrión» (gamemaster mode, shown while a game runs or can be undone): skip, block (confirm), undo, «Cambiar pregunta» (‹ no vista / vista ›), «Saltar a nivel» (‹ n ›), «Dificultad y paquetes» (new GameSettings.svelte, nested modal scope, BundleSelector; refusals stay in the dialog), choice line; jokers column edits uses left (limit = used + left; lib/api fetchJokersUsed, engine jokersUsed). Strings overlay.cheats/replace/seen/unseen/level/settings/settingsNote/apply/used; overlay.left gone; overlay.restart now «Terminar partida (configurar otra)». No more ''Volver al inicio'' after restart; «Reportar pregunta» item was already gone (decision 60).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (35, 'Translation prompts and markets per locale (plan 66)', 'answered', '["approve as drafted", "changes (say which)"]', 'Plan 66 (`plan 66: Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)`) needs new prompt texts; prompts are the gamemaster''s (D-36). Task 437 drafted them; they are staged but unused until tasks 438–440 wire them in. Approve, or answer with changes.

## What is proposed
- **Markets:**
  - `en`: US + UK families; US spelling and dates; metric first, imperial in brackets where natural; "a"/"an" must fit all options.
  - `de`: Germany, Austria, Switzerland; standard German spelled as in Germany (`ß`); words of Germany where they differ; "du"/"ihr"; metric; numbers like Spanish (space from 10 000, decimal comma); articles/case endings must fit all options.
- **Run sizes:** `TRANSLATE_SIZE` = 300 sources per run; the first run of a locale (pilot, QT-5) = 50, then the stop until `qgen health ack tr-<locale>-1`.
- **Review/audit answers** for translation runs in English (`feedback`, `fix`, `notes`); a `fix` changes only the translation, never the Spanish source.
- **No new problem kinds:** translation problems map to the existing ones (fidelity → `fact`/`ambiguity`/`giveaway`, unnatural wording → `style`, Spanish text in media naming the answer → `media`).
- **`travels: no` reasons:** `wordplay`, `about_spanish`, `needs_local_knowledge`, `other`.

## House style and `prompt()` (applied by task 438 after approval, not now)
The "Language" block moves verbatim into `prompts/locale-es.md`; house style keeps `{locale}`, filled per locale. Output for Spanish runs stays byte-identical.

```diff
--- a/authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md
 ## Language
-- All content is in Spanish. The voice depends on the question''s bundle:
-{voices}
-- Neutral means: … (unchanged)
-- Use Colombian references where they fit naturally … (unchanged)
-- Numbers (all bundles): … (unchanged)
+{locale}
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-es.md
+(the five removed lines above, verbatim)
--- a/authoring/tools/qgen.py
+++ b/authoring/tools/qgen.py
-def prompt(*names):
+def prompt(*names, locale="es"):
     """Prompt files joined; {age_groups} and {players} are filled from app/data/age-groups.json,
-    {voices} from app/data/bundles.json."""
+    {locale} from prompts/locale-<locale>.md, {voices} from app/data/bundles.json."""
 …
     text = "\n\n".join((PROMPTS / f"{n}.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8") for n in names)
+    text = text.replace("{locale}", (PROMPTS / f"locale-{locale}.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8").rstrip())
     return (text.replace("{age_groups}", …)
```
Use in locale runs: `prompt("house-style", "translate", locale=L)`; `prompt("house-style", "rate", locale=L)`; `prompt("house-style", "review", "translate-review", locale=L)`; `prompt("house-style", "audit", "translate-review", locale=L)`.

## Drafts (staged)
```diff
diff --git a/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-de.md b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-de.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..37432c2
