@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Task: translate questions
+
+You translate approved Spanish questions of the trivia game described above into the language of the "Language" section, for its players. The Spanish questions were written, rated, fact-checked and reviewed already. Your translation is rated, fact-checked and reviewed again. Adapt, don''t translate literally: the players must meet the same question as a Spanish family does, in natural words of their own language.
+
+## Input
+A list of questions from one subcategory, each with its `id`, `subcategory`, `difficulty`, the text fields (`description`, `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers`, `hints`, `fun_fact`) and its `media` (type, role, and the title and description of the file the players see).
+
+## Keep
+- **The same question:** the same fact, the same correct answer, the same clue. Don''t add facts, don''t drop a detail that makes the question unambiguous, don''t make it easier or harder on purpose.
+- **The same answer**, in the form the players know it: "Cristóbal Colón" → "Christopher Columbus"; a film or book by its release title in the market ("Intensa-Mente" → "Inside Out"). A name without a form of its own stays as it is ("Gabriel García Márquez", "arepa").
+- **Don''t fix the source.** If a Spanish fact looks wrong to you, translate it anyway and say so in `notes` ("source fact doubtful: …").
+
+## Adapt
+- **Units, numbers, dates, spelling:** as the "Language" section says.
+- **Idioms:** an idiom becomes the target language''s idiom, or plain words; never a literal copy.
+- **Wrong answers:** each one stays plausible, the same form and similar length as the answer, and clearly wrong. After translating, check the four options again in the target language:
+  - none became correct or a synonym of the answer (two Spanish words can share one translation);
+  - none stands out by grammar: an article ("a"/"an", "der"/"die"/"das"), a gender or case ending that fits only one option;
+  - none became absurd.
+  Replace a wrong answer that fails with another of the same kind, and say so in `notes`.
+- **Hints:** keep the order from vague to strong. A hint that plays on the Spanish word (first letter, rhyme, syllables, gender, a Spanish saying) is rewritten to do the same job in the target language. Hint 3 must not contain the answer in the target language.
+- **Description:** rewrite the joke so it is funny in the target language: the same idea where it works, a new joke about the same content where it doesn''t. It must not give the answer away or rule out options; watch articles and genders here too.
+- **Fun fact:** translated, units adapted.
+- **Length:** house style "Keep it short" holds in the target language; don''t pad.
+- **Media mentioned in the text** ("Escucha:…", "En la foto…") is translated naturally. The file stays as it is.
+
+## Doesn''t travel
+Some questions can''t be asked fairly in the target language. Then answer `travels: "no"`, give the reason and leave the text fields empty:
+- `wordplay`: the question or its clue lives on a Spanish pun or sound that can''t be rebuilt;
+- `about_spanish`: it asks about the Spanish language itself (a spelling, a Spanish plural, what a Spanish word means);
+- `needs_local_knowledge`: the answer only makes sense to someone who lives in the Spanish-speaking world;
+- `other`: say what in `notes`.
+Don''t give up early: a language question with a clean equivalent travels (the word for opposites → "antonym"), and a question that is only harder for these players travels too (the rater re-rates it). Don''t force one that doesn''t: a strained translation costs more than a missing question.
+
+## Media text
+`media_text`: true when the title or description suggests the file shows Spanish text the players would read (a sign, a poster, a book cover, a caption), or essential audio has spoken Spanish; else false. Answer it for every question; it doesn''t change your translation.
+
+## Answer
+For every input `id`, one item:
+- `id`; `travels`: `"yes"` or `"no"`; `reason`: empty for yes, else one of the reasons above.
+- `description`, `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers` (3), `hints` (3), `fun_fact`: in the target language; empty when `travels` is no.
+- `media_text`: as above.
+- `notes`: in English, one short line per adaptation that a reviewer should know about (a unit changed, a wrong answer replaced, a hint rewritten, a doubtful source fact); empty if you only translated.
```', 'Approve as drafted, except: text in media (Spanish or any language) is never a problem. Drop media_text from translate.md and translate-review.md (no flag, no ''media'' problem for text in media; the ''Media text'' sections go).', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:18:26Z', '2026-10-12T22:11:11Z', 437, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 438: 2026-10-12, task 438: media_text dropped from translate.md, translate-review.md and TRANSLATE_SCHEMA (no media_text in the locale file or the tr-* report); house-style.md Language block → prompts/locale-es.md, prompt(..., locale=) fills {locale}; qgen translate (TRANSLATE_SCHEMA, chunks of 15 per subcategory), rate/factcheck/merge read run.json locale; a re-translated stale entry keeps its old review as top-level previous.

2026-10-12, task 441: 2026-10-12, task 441: docs follow the answer: D-87 (plans/decisions.md) says text in media is never a problem (no media_text flag, no media problem); 15b''s ''Media'' bullet no longer says the review flags visible text per locale; QC.md''s translation-run checks say the same. RUNBOOK, QC.md, directory.md, AGENTS.md, 15b (QT-2, QT-3 [x]) describe qgen batch --translate.

2026-10-13, task 443: 2026-10-12, task 443: no media-text route and no media_text in GET /api/questions?locale=; task 444''s media_text toggle removed from its body');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (36, 'GameRow.locale: written only for non-es games?', 'answered', '[]', 'Keeps the family''s saves and the Python fixture replay byte-identical (plan 68: the family''s game stays as today). The lib layer runs ''new'' on the language''s pool (scope next), every other route on the newest game''s locale; newGame throws if the pool''s locale differs from language.questions.', 'Yes: newGame writes locale only when it isn''t es; missing = es', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:41:19Z', '2026-10-12T19:41:19Z', 449, NULL, 'rule', 449, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (37, 'Per-locale content targets and gap aiming', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 70 (CT-4). D-75 fixes one mix for every language; the simulation is information only (pm decision 21); per-level mix already covers age-group windows (D-76). Translations can only fill a locale from es sources, so the source shortfall is the one new input to D-54''s weights.', 'Every launch language uses targets.json base''s numbers (D-75), deficits counted per locale; no per-mode, per-age-group or per-preset targets; simulation bottlenecks are information; once es meets its target, the en/de source shortfall drives es drafting', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:46:07Z', '2026-10-12T19:46:07Z', 248, NULL, 'rule', 248, '2026-10-12, task 462: 2026-10-12, task 462: targets.deficits(..., locale), source_supply/source_shortfall/draft_gaps in targets.py; target_weights and batches.subcategories use draft_gaps; qgen report --locale, --simulate target check, --cost (es sources past target) per locale; D-84 in plans/decisions.md; --translate weight is task 464.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (38, 'Base bundles and bundle languages', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 71, D-85 in plans/decisions.md. Supersedes D-68''s ''every always_on bundle is always on'' and its auto-adding of base: [] and [colombia] are refused (base_bundle_count). A bundle not listed for the game''s locale is refused (bundle_not_offered). qgen validate: errors for missing/invalid languages, leftover always_on, unknown kind, a launch language without a base bundle; warnings for listed bundles without approved questions in pool.<locale>.json and approved questions of unlisted bundles.', 'kind: base replaces always_on; exactly one base bundle per session; bundles offered per languages; default = the locale''s first base bundle plus every non-base bundle offered in the locale; stored choices that no longer resolve read as the locale''s defaults (never written back)', NULL, '2026-10-12T20:39:19Z', '2026-10-12T20:39:19Z', 481, NULL, 'rule', 481, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (39, 'Local builds start offline?', 'answered', '["both pass", "issues (fill the tables)"]', 'Start test of the local desktop builds (SW-5, plan 56), build commit 06c39dc (version 0.1.0).
