- Question language `en` and `de` (Esc menu, language): the screen lists only `base`.
  - No en/de pools ship yet; throw-away ones (base questions, Spanish text re-labelled):
    `python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open(''app/data/pool.json''));d[''questions'']=[q for q in d[''questions''] if q.get(''bundle'',''base'')==''base''];[json.dump(d,open(f''app/data/pool.{l}.json'',''w'')) for l in (''en'',''de'')]"`
  - Remove afterwards (not gitignored, don''t commit them): `rm app/data/pool.en.json app/data/pool.de.json`, then set the language back to es.
- Overlay shows group and bundles; undo and abandon keep the choice.

Answer "problems": list each one; the close-out (task 479) turns them into fix tasks in plan 71, 29 or 27.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T00:47:47Z', NULL, 478, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (51, '«Solo o en grupo»: which bundles does a game play?', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 13 gives solo the age group only (no configure screen); bundles weren''t specified. Task 378 hides the bundle rows in solo and sends the defaults explicitly, so supply check and game agree; pm decision 33''s fresh default (base only) stays a configure-screen rule.', 'The question language''s default bundles (decision 38): first base bundle plus every other bundle offered; no bundle choice on the Choice screen in solo', NULL, '2026-10-13T01:02:55Z', '2026-10-13T01:02:55Z', 378, NULL, 'rule', 378, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (52, 'Safe area on the Question screen: may the credit line and «Respuesta final» sit in the bottom margin?', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 46''s screen check (task 231) flags them at every size, 1080p included, since the layout is all --u and 16:9 = 16:10 by width. The layout passed the TV overscan check (UI-6, VD-9); the Deck has no overscan. Moving them would change the approved TV look and push the long credit line into the button.', 'Yes: both stay where the TV-tested layout puts them (credit at 0.3 safe-y, the candy button''s last ~0.2 u in the 4 % margin); every other text stays inside the safe area', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:06:10Z', '2026-10-13T02:06:10Z', 231, NULL, 'rule', 231, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (53, 'Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?', 'answered', '["Keys in the catalog per language (joker.<id>.key, flag.key, screen.question.replayKey, screen.start.newKey, mode/customize keys), mnemonic for the name, collision rule checked per catalog; es unchanged", "Neutral 1–5 row for the jokers in every language (conflicts with pick n)", "F1–F5 for the jokers in every language"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-4, `plans/15a-ui-translation.md`). The shortcut letters are already catalog leaves; `en.ts` still uses the `es` letters for jokers. This decides whether every language picks its own letters.

Current keys (`app/client/src/locales/es.ts`):
- Question screen: answers `A`–`D`; jokers `joker.<id>.key`: Soplo `S`, Paso `P`, Bájale `F`, Cambiazo `T`, Francotirador `X`; replay `screen.question.replayKey` `R`
- every screen: flag `flag.key` `M`, Esc menu, Enter/Space confirm, Backspace back, `1`–`9` = `pick n` (Select cards)
- Start: new game `screen.start.newKey` `N`
- Choice: `mode.gamemasterKey` `A`, `mode.soloKey` `G`, `customize.openKey` `P` (`en`: `G`, `A`, `C`); bundle letters fill in around them

Collision rule per catalog (checked by `check:literals`, task 454): every key a single letter; unique among the keys live on the same screen; not `A`–`D` where answers are shown; no digit (`pick n`).

Why option 1:
- `toIntent` matches `e.key`, not the key position, so letters work on QWERTZ/AZERTY; position-based neutral rows (`Q W E R T` on QWERTY) move around on those layouts
- mnemonic letters keep the on-screen key next to the joker name readable (`S` for Soplo)
- pads use focus and face buttons anyway (decision 9: Gamepad on the Question screen), so keys only matter for keyboard players

Against 2: digits are `pick n` already. Against 3: `F1`–`F5` are awkward on laptops (Fn layer) and the Steam Deck, and clash with browser/OS keys (F1 help, F5 reload, F11 fullscreen).', 'Keys in the catalog per language (joker.<id>.key, flag.key, screen.question.replayKey, screen.start.newKey, mode/customize keys), mnemonic for the name, collision rule checked per catalog; es unchanged', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:07:43Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: D-91: shortcut keys per catalog; en jokers H P F K T, de Z N G W F, es/es-ES unchanged S P F T X; check:literals key rule per catalog passes; D-89''s ''keys stay S P F T X'' no longer holds');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (54, 'German name for the hint joker «Soplo»?', 'answered', '["Spickzettel (S)", "Psst! (P)", "Zaunpfahl (Z)", "Eselsbrücke (E)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Soplo», English «Hint» (decision 40: English name for the hint joker «Soplo»)
- What it does: shows a hint for the current question («Soplo {n}» notes); can be played again for the next hint
- Why: «Spickzettel» (crib note) is the school-cheating image behind «Soplo», family-friendly, keeps `S`; «Psst!» is the whisper itself; «Zaunpfahl» from «Wink mit dem Zaunpfahl» (a heavy-handed hint); «Eselsbrücke» (memory aid) is warm but less about being told', 'Zaunpfahl (Z)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:02Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: hint joker «Zaunpfahl» (Z), hint note «Zaunpfahl {n}», spent error (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (55, 'German name for the skip joker «Paso»?', 'answered', '["Weg damit! (W)", "Ich passe (I)", "Tschüss! (U)", "Nächste! (N, collides with screen.start.newKey only on Start)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

