- What it does: skips the question; optionally purges its topic for the rest of the game (stamp «ELIMINADO»). The dialog''s plain option is `joker.skip.pass` («Paso» / «Just pass»), German draft «Nur passen»
- Why: «Weg damit!» covers both skip and purge with attitude; «Ich passe» is the card-game phrase, closest to «Paso»; «Tschüss!» and «Nächste!» are cheeky but say only one half', 'Näxt (N)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:02Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: skip joker «Näxt» (N), purge line «Näxt, und tschüss, Thema „{name}“», spent error; plain option stays «Nur passen» (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (56, 'German name for the easier joker «Bájale»?', 'answered', '["Gang runter (G)", "Halblang (H)", "Kinderspiel (K)", "Sachte! (S, collides with Spickzettel)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

