- Why: «Gang runter» (shift down a gear, «einen Gang runterschalten» = take it easy) matches the dial animation; «Halblang» from «Mach mal halblang!» is the colloquial «bájale»; «Kinderspiel» (child''s play) says what you get; «Sachte!» is short and soft', 'Gang runter (G)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:02Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: easier joker «Gang runter», key F → G (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (57, 'German name for the category joker «Cambiazo»?', 'answered', '["Extrawurst (E)", "Wunschthema (W)", "Kehrtwende (K)", "Themenhopser (T)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Cambiazo», English «Ms Picky» (decision 43: English name for the category joker «Cambiazo»)
- What it does: the players pick another topic; the question is replaced by one of that topic (picker title «Cambiazo: ¿qué tema quieren?»)
- Why: «Extrawurst» («eine Extrawurst wollen» = demanding special treatment) is the German «picky», very idiomatic; «Wunschthema» (topic of your choice) is the plainest; «Kehrtwende» (U-turn) is the swap; «Themenhopser» a playful topic hop', 'Wunschzeit (W)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:03Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: category joker «Wunschzeit» (W), picker title «Wunschzeit: Welches Thema wollt ihr?», spent error (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (58, 'German name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?', 'answered', '["Scharfschütze (X)", "Kunstschuss (K)", "Blattschuss (B is an answer key: X)", "Meisterschuss (M is flag.key: X)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Francotirador», English «Trick Shot» (decision 44: English name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»)
- What it does: the players aim at the answer they think is false; if it is, that answer is gone; if they hit the correct one, the level repeats
- Why: «Scharfschütze» is the clearest image (aim, shoot), exactly 13 characters; «Kunstschuss» is «Trick Shot»; «Blattschuss» (the clean hunting shot) is idiomatic; «Meisterschuss» (masterstroke) is flattering. `X` stays possible as a crosshair key in any of them', 'Finte (F)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:03Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:57Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: snipe joker «Finte» (F), spent error «keine Finte mehr übrig» (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (59, 'Neutral Spanish UI wording in es.ts (D-78)?', 'answered', '["Apply all (1 and 2)", "Apply listed subset (name the numbers)", "Keep as is"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5), decision 27: Spanish variety (OQ-31): `es` is neutral Latin American Spanish (es-419); `es-ES` overrides only where Spain differs. Scan of `app/client/src/locales/es.ts` (every leaf) for Colombian wording; the family sees these lines.

Old → new:
