Comment only, no screen change: the header comment of `es.ts` says «Colombian usage»; task 455 rewords it to es-419.', 'Apply all (1 and 2)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:10Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:57Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: es.ts: copy.consolation.9 «¡Qué maravilla!», overlay.confirm «Presiona otra vez»; es-ES keeps «Pulsa»; es.ts header says es-419 (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (60, 'One mechanism for questions with problems: flag or report?', 'answered', '[]', 'Gamemaster, after D25 play-test 2026-10-13: flag (M, GM-5) and «Reportar pregunta» (MD-6) overlap and it isn''t clear where each goes; flag only reached trivia-authoring at its next start, report never. Gamemaster likes the flag icon; wants the report''s dialog on it.', 'Flag only, with a dialog. The flag icon and its key (flag.key, M in es) open a confirm dialog like «Reportar pregunta»''s, with an optional free-text description of the issue. The separate overlay item «Reportar pregunta» goes. One save entry per flag (question, player, level, date, optional note).', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:50:43Z', '2026-10-13T02:50:43Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13: Follow-up task in plan 59: merge report into flag; trivia-authoring turns flags into needs-work with the note as feedback; the list with «Copiar» stays for players without authoring tools.

2026-10-13, task 625: 2026-10-13, task 625: FlagDialog.svelte (flag icon / M / pad Select: optional note, Enter flags, Esc/⌫ cancel; flagged: save note or «Quitar marca»; pad: LetterPicker note mode with picker.letters/marks per catalog); overlay item and engine action report gone; FlagList.svelte «Preguntas marcadas» with notes + Copiar; save v4: reports merged into flags {flagged_on, player, level?, note?} (parseSave, save.py, save_file.flags for v3); apply_flags feedback «Marcada en el juego (player, date): <note>», ledger stamp includes the note so an edited note applies again');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (61, 'hyphens: auto only for German UI (LUI-5)', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 69 asks for hyphens: auto on text blocks and no per-language CSS unless unavoidable. Chromium hyphenates Spanish line ends too (checked in headless Chromium 147), so a global rule would rehyphenate the family''s es screens (question cards, explanations); es must stay pixel-identical. Scoping to :lang(de) is the one exception; <html lang> comes from plan 68.', '.game:lang(de) { hyphens: auto } in theme.css; es/en keep no hyphenation', NULL, '2026-10-13T04:31:46Z', '2026-10-13T04:31:46Z', 456, NULL, 'rule', 456, '');
